1
00:00:56,169 --> 00:00:59,053
Thank you.
Thank you.

2
00:00:59,122 --> 00:01:00,789
The band...

3
00:01:08,665 --> 00:01:11,182
Mommy, please don't go.

4
00:01:11,251 --> 00:01:13,718
Don't worry, Gerda.

5
00:01:13,787 --> 00:01:16,505
I'll be back soon.

6
00:01:16,573 --> 00:01:19,373
Stay and make sure Daddy plays
all the right notes, okay?

7
00:01:23,546 --> 00:01:27,181
Goodbye. I love you.
All right, gentlemen?

8
00:02:09,659 --> 00:02:13,077
It's all right, sultan.
Nothing to fear, just
a little wind.

9
00:02:17,284 --> 00:02:18,949
It's all right.
It's all right.

10
00:02:29,029 --> 00:02:30,895
It's all right.
It's all right.

11
00:03:09,920 --> 00:03:12,770
Amy?

12
00:03:12,839 --> 00:03:17,308
Amy!

13
00:03:17,377 --> 00:03:19,594
Amy!

14
00:03:25,268 --> 00:03:26,918
Amy!

15
00:03:40,066 --> 00:03:42,217
We'll have to give up
the search for tonight,

16
00:03:42,285 --> 00:03:44,970
otherwise, someone else
is going to be lost.

17
00:03:45,038 --> 00:03:47,038
No, no.

18
00:03:47,107 --> 00:03:48,239
I'll not
leave her here.

19
00:03:48,308 --> 00:03:50,074
Go home!

20
00:03:50,143 --> 00:03:52,977
Take the child with you.
Everybody go home.

21
00:03:55,349 --> 00:03:58,065
I'll not
leave her here.

22
00:04:13,700 --> 00:04:16,567
Oh, Gerda.
Oh...

23
00:04:16,636 --> 00:04:18,002
Thank you.
Come on—

24
00:04:18,071 --> 00:04:20,138
let's get you inside
and get you warm.

25
00:04:26,647 --> 00:04:28,813
Thank you for all
your help, gentlemen.

26
00:04:28,882 --> 00:04:31,482
Of course.

27
00:04:31,551 --> 00:04:33,785
I'm sure Wolfgang
will find her.

28
00:04:33,853 --> 00:04:36,086
Yes, he will.

29
00:04:36,155 --> 00:04:39,107
Amy!
Amy!

30
00:04:40,026 --> 00:04:42,693
Amy!
Amy!

31
00:04:59,545 --> 00:05:03,247
Amy...

32
00:05:03,316 --> 00:05:04,549
Amy!

33
00:05:04,617 --> 00:05:06,617
Mommy?

34
00:05:08,121 --> 00:05:11,890
Mommy? Mommy!

35
00:05:11,975 --> 00:05:14,408
Amy!

36
00:05:14,461 --> 00:05:15,526
Mommy?

37
00:05:30,460 --> 00:05:32,010
Mommy?

38
00:06:48,521 --> 00:06:51,088
Good night, Daddy.

39
00:07:18,952 --> 00:07:21,119
Good morning, Daddy.

40
00:07:38,171 --> 00:07:40,621
Kai, your hours
will be from dawn

41
00:07:40,690 --> 00:07:43,224
until the last guest
goes to bed.

42
00:07:43,293 --> 00:07:45,893
If my guests decide
to stay up all night,

43
00:07:45,962 --> 00:07:48,362
so shall you.
When I summon you,

44
00:07:48,431 --> 00:07:51,515
you will be here
before this bell...

45
00:07:51,584 --> 00:07:56,420
stops ringing,
no matter where you are,
no matter what you are doing.

46
00:07:56,489 --> 00:07:57,856
You understand?

47
00:07:57,924 --> 00:08:00,558
Yes, sir.

48
00:08:00,627 --> 00:08:02,042
Kai,

49
00:08:02,111 --> 00:08:05,913
tardiness in any shape or form
will not be tolerated.

50
00:08:06,849 --> 00:08:08,115
Do you understand?

51
00:08:08,185 --> 00:08:09,500
I understand, sir.

52
00:08:09,568 --> 00:08:12,469
I thought you'd
be here yesterday.

53
00:08:12,555 --> 00:08:15,823
Oh, well, I... had
no money for the coach, sir,

54
00:08:15,892 --> 00:08:17,725
so I had to walk
over the mountains.

55
00:08:21,631 --> 00:08:23,380
Why are you
smiling?

56
00:08:23,449 --> 00:08:26,301
Just pleased
to be here, sir.

57
00:09:04,874 --> 00:09:06,857
Bellboy...

58
00:09:07,827 --> 00:09:10,178
Bellboy!

59
00:09:17,736 --> 00:09:19,837
Good day, sir.

60
00:09:35,388 --> 00:09:36,954
Bellboy!

61
00:11:08,264 --> 00:11:10,264
I'm Kai.

62
00:11:10,332 --> 00:11:12,199
Yes, I know.

63
00:12:17,049 --> 00:12:19,016
Not acceptable...

64
00:12:19,085 --> 00:12:22,669
Not in the white bear hotel.
Do it the proper way.

65
00:12:22,738 --> 00:12:24,788
Yes, Mr. Hahn.

66
00:13:04,780 --> 00:13:06,997
Oh, hello.

67
00:13:07,066 --> 00:13:09,700
Look at those.
Aren't they beautiful?

68
00:13:16,125 --> 00:13:17,925
They're gorgeous.

69
00:13:19,629 --> 00:13:21,795
Why don't you
buy them?

70
00:13:21,864 --> 00:13:24,131
Oh, I don't
need them.

71
00:13:24,199 --> 00:13:26,800
I was just
admiring them.

72
00:13:29,238 --> 00:13:32,589
It's the first snow.

73
00:13:32,658 --> 00:13:34,558
Hope it settles.

74
00:13:37,379 --> 00:13:38,512
What's wrong?

75
00:13:38,580 --> 00:13:40,647
Nothing.

76
00:13:40,716 --> 00:13:45,119
I just hate winter,
that's all.

77
00:13:58,183 --> 00:14:01,485
Pretzels!
Hot pretzels!

78
00:14:26,145 --> 00:14:28,479
I think
she likes you.

79
00:14:32,718 --> 00:14:34,818
I, uh...

80
00:14:34,887 --> 00:14:37,621
It's all right, Kai.

81
00:14:37,690 --> 00:14:39,490
You and Gerda would make
a splendid couple.

82
00:14:39,559 --> 00:14:42,309
Well, tell
her father that.

83
00:14:42,378 --> 00:14:44,177
Oh, he'll come around.

84
00:14:44,246 --> 00:14:47,280
He's been unhappy for so long,
he's bound to sooner or later.

85
00:14:54,974 --> 00:14:58,275
Minna, why is it that Gerda
hates the winter so much?

86
00:14:58,344 --> 00:15:05,048
It took her mother's life
and her father's joy

87
00:15:05,117 --> 00:15:07,584
all in one night.

88
00:15:11,791 --> 00:15:15,259
What are you going to do
for your 18th birthday?

89
00:15:15,327 --> 00:15:17,311
Your father would let you
have a party, you know,

90
00:15:17,380 --> 00:15:18,312
if you asked him.

91
00:15:18,380 --> 00:15:19,930
Do you think so?

92
00:15:19,999 --> 00:15:22,566
I'll tell him
he has to.

93
00:15:22,634 --> 00:15:25,302
It's been far too long
since we had a party here.

94
00:15:25,371 --> 00:15:27,672
And you can invite
your boyfriend.

95
00:15:27,740 --> 00:15:29,623
He's not my boyfriend.

96
00:15:35,031 --> 00:15:38,498
Your mother
used to look at me like that...

97
00:15:38,567 --> 00:15:40,651
And she couldn't lie
about her feelings either.

98
00:15:45,657 --> 00:15:47,908
Did I put pepper in this
already?

99
00:15:47,977 --> 00:15:49,276
Twice, at least.

100
00:15:49,345 --> 00:15:51,845
Oh...

101
00:15:51,914 --> 00:15:57,485
Gerda, why don't you wear
your mother's rose brooch?

102
00:15:57,553 --> 00:15:59,253
She'd want you to.

103
00:16:05,060 --> 00:16:06,927
Do you remember
how it was always

104
00:16:06,995 --> 00:16:09,262
warm to the touch
when you were a child?

105
00:16:09,315 --> 00:16:11,548
She made it magic.

106
00:16:11,617 --> 00:16:13,884
I know why it was warm.

107
00:16:13,952 --> 00:16:16,853
She used to put it on the stove
before she kissed me good night.

108
00:16:16,922 --> 00:16:20,657
No— it was magic.

109
00:16:26,182 --> 00:16:29,283
And it's not meant
to sit in a drawer.

110
00:18:45,854 --> 00:18:47,921
So how are you
liking it here, Kai?

111
00:18:47,990 --> 00:18:51,725
Well, let me see.
Apart from 20-hour workdays,

112
00:18:51,777 --> 00:18:53,410
the endless lifting
of heavy luggage,

113
00:18:53,479 --> 00:18:56,079
the chopping
of rock-hard firewood,

114
00:18:56,149 --> 00:18:58,082
the hauling
of heavy laundry,

115
00:18:58,150 --> 00:19:02,169
and, of course, the cleaning
of endless muddy boots,
I like it just fine.

116
00:19:03,739 --> 00:19:07,173
Sounds like
he's coming this way.
You'd better scoot.

117
00:19:07,242 --> 00:19:09,026
Where's that bellboy?

118
00:19:09,095 --> 00:19:11,144
Kai!

119
00:19:13,498 --> 00:19:15,865
Minna, have you seen
the bellboy?

120
00:19:15,935 --> 00:19:17,801
The guests are asking
for their boots.

121
00:19:17,869 --> 00:19:20,103
No, I haven't
seen him lately,
though I expect

122
00:19:20,172 --> 00:19:23,023
the boots will be here
soon enough, nice and clean.

123
00:19:24,477 --> 00:19:26,009
Minna, you should
check that stew.

124
00:19:26,078 --> 00:19:28,796
It does not smell
up to your usual standard.

125
00:19:28,864 --> 00:19:30,998
Likely just needs
a little bit of seasoning.

126
00:19:32,117 --> 00:19:34,618
I'll see to it.

127
00:19:38,791 --> 00:19:40,190
Wolfgang...

128
00:19:40,258 --> 00:19:41,492
Hmm?

129
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:43,477
You know,
he's not a bad boy.

130
00:19:43,545 --> 00:19:45,412
Meaning?

131
00:19:45,481 --> 00:19:48,248
Haven't you seen the way
he and Gerda look at each other?

132
00:19:50,335 --> 00:19:53,237
And why shouldn't he?
He's a nice young man,

133
00:19:53,306 --> 00:19:55,238
and she's
a most attractive girl.

134
00:19:55,307 --> 00:19:56,456
She's a...

135
00:19:57,392 --> 00:19:59,059
Young woman.

136
00:20:05,784 --> 00:20:07,951
Bellboy.

137
00:20:08,020 --> 00:20:09,319
Yes, sir?

138
00:20:09,388 --> 00:20:10,871
What do you know
about that?

139
00:20:14,510 --> 00:20:16,293
Uh, nothing, sir.

140
00:21:24,045 --> 00:21:25,796
No.

141
00:21:25,864 --> 00:21:27,081
No!

142
00:21:50,556 --> 00:21:53,990
Uh, Gerda...

143
00:21:54,059 --> 00:21:57,060
Listen, do you want
to come skating with me
after work tonight?

144
00:21:57,129 --> 00:21:58,662
No.

145
00:21:58,731 --> 00:22:00,497
I'm not really
any good.

146
00:22:00,566 --> 00:22:01,765
Well, I could
teach you.

147
00:22:01,834 --> 00:22:03,216
I don't skate anymore.

148
00:22:03,285 --> 00:22:04,835
Why not?

149
00:22:04,903 --> 00:22:08,021
I told you,
I don't like winter.

150
00:22:22,504 --> 00:22:24,104
There you are,
winter's finished.

151
00:22:25,457 --> 00:22:28,174
So if I step outside,
there'll be daffodils everywhere

152
00:22:28,243 --> 00:22:29,610
and all the snow
will be gone?

153
00:22:54,603 --> 00:22:57,103
Didn't you
promise me daffodils?

154
00:22:57,172 --> 00:23:00,073
Oh, they're out there.
They're just...

155
00:23:00,142 --> 00:23:01,574
Just a little shy,
that's all.

156
00:23:03,111 --> 00:23:04,611
Maybe if you come
skating with me,

157
00:23:04,680 --> 00:23:05,912
they'll come out.

158
00:23:12,655 --> 00:23:14,854
I'm warning you,
I'm not very good.

159
00:23:14,923 --> 00:23:16,523
I haven't been
on skates in years.

160
00:23:16,592 --> 00:23:18,425
You'll be fine.

161
00:23:25,767 --> 00:23:28,085
Come on, try it.
It's easy.

162
00:23:30,222 --> 00:23:32,339
Come on.

163
00:23:32,407 --> 00:23:34,508
Hey, maybe one little spin
is all it will take

164
00:23:34,577 --> 00:23:36,142
for the daffodils
to come up.

165
00:23:36,211 --> 00:23:38,579
Oh, well,
if the daffodils insist...

166
00:23:38,647 --> 00:23:40,080
Are you all right?

167
00:23:40,148 --> 00:23:41,281
I'm fine.

168
00:23:41,350 --> 00:23:42,766
I'm so sorry.
It was my fault.

169
00:23:42,835 --> 00:23:44,100
Really, Kai,
it's all right.

170
00:23:45,170 --> 00:23:48,521
I just don't want to do
any more spins.

171
00:23:48,590 --> 00:23:51,124
Okay, agreed, then,
no more spins.

172
00:23:56,198 --> 00:23:57,964
are you all right?

173
00:23:58,033 --> 00:24:00,167
I think so.

174
00:24:38,340 --> 00:24:40,323
you know, for someone
who can't skate,

175
00:24:40,392 --> 00:24:43,043
you were pretty
impressive...

176
00:24:43,111 --> 00:24:46,496
And the prettiest girl
on the whole lake.

177
00:24:46,565 --> 00:24:48,732
I was the only girl
on the whole lake.

178
00:24:48,801 --> 00:24:50,734
Which, I'd like
to point out,

179
00:24:50,803 --> 00:24:53,954
was entirely devoid
of daffodils.

180
00:24:54,022 --> 00:24:56,589
They're still just a little
uncertain about you, that's all.

181
00:25:00,713 --> 00:25:04,147
Although...

182
00:25:07,036 --> 00:25:08,852
Bellboy!

183
00:25:16,311 --> 00:25:19,462
Bellboy!

184
00:25:28,189 --> 00:25:30,123
I'm right here.

185
00:25:30,191 --> 00:25:32,225
Don't make me
go backwards.

186
00:26:07,812 --> 00:26:10,229
I'm going to get
some chestnuts.

187
00:26:13,635 --> 00:26:16,119
That's fine.
Thank you.

188
00:26:17,489 --> 00:26:18,789
What?

189
00:26:18,857 --> 00:26:21,191
Gerda,
I just...

190
00:26:22,427 --> 00:26:23,827
Duck!

191
00:26:28,316 --> 00:26:30,083
You were saying?

192
00:26:30,135 --> 00:26:32,319
Well, I was
about to say

193
00:26:32,387 --> 00:26:34,488
I think you should
give winter a second chance,

194
00:26:34,556 --> 00:26:35,788
although now
I'm not so sure.

195
00:27:33,081 --> 00:27:35,515
I bet you used to do this a lot
with all the other girls

196
00:27:35,584 --> 00:27:36,967
on the other side
of the mountain.

197
00:27:37,035 --> 00:27:39,769
I did...

198
00:27:39,838 --> 00:27:43,873
But they were
my sisters.

199
00:27:43,942 --> 00:27:47,443
My parents died
when I was quite young,

200
00:27:47,512 --> 00:27:51,381
so it was up to me
to entertain my sisters.

201
00:27:51,449 --> 00:27:54,067
Your sisters
were very lucky.

202
00:27:57,089 --> 00:27:59,422
Listen, I know
your father doesn't think

203
00:27:59,491 --> 00:28:01,758
I'm good enough
for you, but...

204
00:28:41,983 --> 00:28:46,018
I love you, Gerda.

205
00:28:46,087 --> 00:28:47,354
I...

206
00:28:54,696 --> 00:28:56,763
We'd better get back.

207
00:28:58,133 --> 00:29:00,116
It's just snow.
It can't hurt us.

208
00:29:01,470 --> 00:29:04,838
Kai? Kai!
Kai, are you all right?

209
00:29:04,907 --> 00:29:06,489
I've got something
in my eye.

210
00:29:06,558 --> 00:29:07,990
Let me see it.

211
00:29:08,059 --> 00:29:09,992
It's fine.
It's gone now.

212
00:29:10,061 --> 00:29:11,928
Let me look.
It's all bloodshot.

213
00:29:11,996 --> 00:29:14,264
Leave me alone!
I'm not a baby.

214
00:29:17,302 --> 00:29:18,918
Sorry, it just...

215
00:29:20,372 --> 00:29:23,172
It just stings, that's all.

216
00:29:23,242 --> 00:29:24,874
It's gone now. I'm fine.

217
00:29:26,611 --> 00:29:29,261
It was just a piece of ice.

218
00:29:45,481 --> 00:29:48,181
All right, I think
you should go on alone now.

219
00:29:48,249 --> 00:29:50,049
What?

220
00:29:53,605 --> 00:29:55,572
I'm just
thinking of you.

221
00:29:55,640 --> 00:29:57,824
You don't want to have
to explain to your father

222
00:29:57,893 --> 00:29:59,259
when he sees us
together, do you?

223
00:29:59,327 --> 00:30:00,260
But, Kai—

224
00:30:01,396 --> 00:30:03,829
just go on
ahead of me.

225
00:30:05,016 --> 00:30:06,699
It's for the best.
Go on.

226
00:30:06,768 --> 00:30:10,020
If you think so...

227
00:31:35,023 --> 00:31:36,823
What happened?

228
00:31:38,393 --> 00:31:40,242
Mischief makers,
I suppose.

229
00:31:40,311 --> 00:31:44,064
Kai, the other night
at the lake.

230
00:31:44,132 --> 00:31:45,432
I...

231
00:31:45,500 --> 00:31:47,033
I'm sorry, Gerda.

232
00:31:47,101 --> 00:31:50,520
I don't know what happened.
I just...

233
00:31:50,589 --> 00:31:52,855
It's all right.

234
00:31:52,924 --> 00:31:55,224
You don't need
to apologize.

235
00:31:55,294 --> 00:31:57,793
Maybe we can
go again tonight.

236
00:31:57,862 --> 00:31:59,495
I could use
another lesson

237
00:31:59,564 --> 00:32:01,664
from a certain handsome
instructor I know.

238
00:32:09,441 --> 00:32:11,274
Well, he'd better be
a skilled teacher,

239
00:32:11,342 --> 00:32:13,742
because, frankly,
your skating is hopeless

240
00:32:13,811 --> 00:32:16,579
and graceless.

241
00:32:54,152 --> 00:32:56,085
Amazing things,
snowflakes.

242
00:32:58,623 --> 00:33:01,057
There isn't a fault in them.
They're perfect.

243
00:33:01,126 --> 00:33:03,526
If only
they didn't melt.

244
00:33:03,594 --> 00:33:07,447
Why don't you close the window?
It's freezing.

245
00:33:07,499 --> 00:33:10,700
Have you ever
been cut?

246
00:33:10,769 --> 00:33:12,702
What?

247
00:33:12,771 --> 00:33:16,272
With something
really sharp, like...

248
00:33:16,341 --> 00:33:18,307
Like a knife,

249
00:33:18,376 --> 00:33:21,678
like a blade,

250
00:33:21,746 --> 00:33:24,096
like a horrible
piece of ice?

251
00:33:25,467 --> 00:33:28,368
Have you ever been cut?

252
00:33:28,436 --> 00:33:33,005
I don't know
who you are anymore, Kai.

253
00:33:33,074 --> 00:33:35,975
What happened?

254
00:33:57,649 --> 00:33:59,749
I don't know
what I've done wrong.

255
00:33:59,817 --> 00:34:03,752
What have I done
to make him dislike me?

256
00:34:03,821 --> 00:34:05,854
Ask him.

257
00:34:15,783 --> 00:34:17,867
Why have you
become like this?

258
00:34:19,570 --> 00:34:22,755
Why are you
being so horrible?

259
00:34:22,823 --> 00:34:24,907
It's as if you're determined
to turn everyone against you.

260
00:34:24,976 --> 00:34:26,843
They're already
against me.

261
00:34:26,912 --> 00:34:28,444
Your father
treats me like a slave.

262
00:34:28,513 --> 00:34:30,079
He respects you.
I know he does.

263
00:34:30,148 --> 00:34:31,480
Yeah, and one day,

264
00:34:31,549 --> 00:34:33,399
he's going to let me
run the hotel, right?

265
00:34:33,467 --> 00:34:34,400
I don't think so.

266
00:34:34,468 --> 00:34:36,486
It's not like that.

267
00:34:36,554 --> 00:34:38,554
Maybe if you were to stick
to the job...

268
00:34:39,841 --> 00:34:41,290
Hey, Gerda,
I have an idea.

269
00:34:41,359 --> 00:34:43,393
Why don't we follow
the mountains up north,

270
00:34:43,461 --> 00:34:45,812
just you and me,

271
00:34:45,864 --> 00:34:48,848
skating and skating
and skating.

272
00:34:48,917 --> 00:34:50,366
Would you like that?
We could go right now.

273
00:34:50,435 --> 00:34:51,701
We won't tell anybody.
Let's go!

274
00:34:51,770 --> 00:34:54,237
No. I want you
to come back

275
00:34:54,305 --> 00:34:57,073
to the hotel with me
before you get sacked.

276
00:35:01,546 --> 00:35:04,630
Kai...

277
00:35:04,698 --> 00:35:06,732
I don't understand.

278
00:35:06,801 --> 00:35:09,135
You said you loved me.

279
00:35:14,192 --> 00:35:16,392
You never said
you loved me.

280
00:36:09,647 --> 00:36:13,032
Madame...

281
00:36:13,101 --> 00:36:17,269
Good afternoon.
I do apologize.

282
00:36:17,338 --> 00:36:18,971
We weren't expecting
anyone today.

283
00:36:19,040 --> 00:36:20,740
Do you mind
if I ask you

284
00:36:20,809 --> 00:36:22,625
how you made it through
the pass to the village?

285
00:36:22,694 --> 00:36:24,610
The roads have been
closed for days.

286
00:36:24,679 --> 00:36:27,630
Would you be so kind as to have
someone fetch my bags?
They're outside.

287
00:36:27,699 --> 00:36:29,131
<i> Ja, ja.</i>

288
00:36:29,200 --> 00:36:30,133
Bellboy?

289
00:36:30,201 --> 00:36:33,819
Bellboy! Bellboy!

290
00:36:33,888 --> 00:36:37,857
Now, would it be possible for me
to have a room on the top floor?

291
00:36:37,909 --> 00:36:41,861
<i> Ja,</i> the top floor.

292
00:36:41,930 --> 00:36:43,980
How long will you be
staying with us, madame?

293
00:36:44,048 --> 00:36:46,882
Why? Are you expecting
a rush of late-arriving guests?

294
00:36:49,137 --> 00:36:50,302
No.

295
00:36:50,371 --> 00:36:54,406
The storm may continue
for another day.

296
00:36:54,475 --> 00:36:57,326
I thought that perhaps you might
be more comfortable in a suite.

297
00:36:57,395 --> 00:36:59,111
The storm will be
gone tomorrow.

298
00:37:00,331 --> 00:37:02,298
Trust me.

299
00:37:26,574 --> 00:37:29,258
Would you like me to have
some hot tea sent to your room?

300
00:37:29,327 --> 00:37:32,044
No, no tea.
Just a jug of ice water.

301
00:37:32,113 --> 00:37:33,830
I'll have it sent
straight up.

302
00:37:35,600 --> 00:37:37,666
Bellboy!

303
00:37:37,735 --> 00:37:40,285
He's somewhere.

304
00:37:40,354 --> 00:37:41,904
Kai?

305
00:38:07,331 --> 00:38:10,266
Are you going to stand outside
for the rest of your life?

306
00:38:33,708 --> 00:38:35,274
Do you like mirrors?

307
00:38:42,534 --> 00:38:45,218
I was just wondering
whether you knew or not...

308
00:38:45,286 --> 00:38:48,237
And you don't, do you?

309
00:38:59,433 --> 00:39:01,167
What are you doing?

310
00:39:02,637 --> 00:39:04,971
I'm lighting a fire for you.
It's freezing.

311
00:39:05,022 --> 00:39:06,672
Do you think
I'm cold?

312
00:39:08,042 --> 00:39:09,525
Do I look cold
to you?

313
00:39:12,897 --> 00:39:15,464
I'm not cold.

314
00:39:17,768 --> 00:39:21,236
I'm not cold at all.

315
00:39:25,977 --> 00:39:30,513
You've got
lovely eyes.

316
00:39:30,582 --> 00:39:34,083
It's the first thing
I noticed about you.

317
00:39:34,151 --> 00:39:35,785
How old are you?

318
00:39:35,854 --> 00:39:38,721
18.

319
00:39:44,746 --> 00:39:47,179
I think I'm needed
downstairs.

320
00:39:48,866 --> 00:39:51,266
About a month ago,

321
00:39:51,335 --> 00:39:53,686
there was a terrible
snowstorm here.

322
00:39:53,755 --> 00:39:57,940
It was just like today.
It was a blizzard.

323
00:39:58,009 --> 00:39:59,275
Do you know anyone
who was...

324
00:39:59,344 --> 00:40:03,329
How can I put this?

325
00:40:03,398 --> 00:40:06,332
Affected by it?

326
00:40:06,401 --> 00:40:09,668
Anyone who changed?

327
00:40:11,755 --> 00:40:13,189
I don't know
what you mean.

328
00:40:13,257 --> 00:40:16,792
For instance,
have you noticed

329
00:40:16,861 --> 00:40:19,478
what a mean, selfish
little person

330
00:40:19,547 --> 00:40:21,246
you've become
recently?

331
00:40:21,315 --> 00:40:24,216
You know
why that is?

332
00:40:24,285 --> 00:40:27,419
No.

333
00:40:27,488 --> 00:40:30,289
Because you want
something from me.

334
00:40:30,357 --> 00:40:33,459
You crave it
more than anything else.

335
00:40:33,527 --> 00:40:38,698
In fact, you can't
stop thinking about it...

336
00:40:38,766 --> 00:40:41,033
Even though you don't know
what it is.

337
00:40:41,085 --> 00:40:44,570
I'll be on the lake
tonight.

338
00:40:44,639 --> 00:40:46,805
Why don't you come down
and see me?

339
00:40:50,244 --> 00:40:52,010
I can't tonight.

340
00:40:55,900 --> 00:40:58,033
Oh.

341
00:40:58,102 --> 00:41:01,187
What a pity.

342
00:41:01,256 --> 00:41:03,172
I'm only here
for one night.

343
00:41:05,009 --> 00:41:07,660
You like winter,
don't you?

344
00:41:09,346 --> 00:41:10,379
Kai,

345
00:41:10,448 --> 00:41:13,015
come here.

346
00:41:17,688 --> 00:41:20,022
I've got something
for you.

347
00:41:58,629 --> 00:42:01,196
Aren't you even going
to wish me a happy birthday?

348
00:42:06,304 --> 00:42:11,073
I'm sorry.
Yes, Gerda, happy birthday.

349
00:42:11,142 --> 00:42:13,358
Thank you.

350
00:42:13,427 --> 00:42:16,078
I've been awful, I know,
but that's finished.

351
00:42:16,147 --> 00:42:19,949
Forgive me, Gerda.
I've just...

352
00:42:20,017 --> 00:42:23,986
I've been sick, that's all.
Just sick.

353
00:42:24,055 --> 00:42:26,589
Then you'll be
at my party tonight?

354
00:42:26,657 --> 00:42:28,590
Don't let me down.

355
00:42:28,659 --> 00:42:32,445
Daddy didn't want you there
after the way you've been.

356
00:42:32,513 --> 00:42:34,263
I'll be there,
I promise.

357
00:42:34,332 --> 00:42:38,684
I'll never forgive you
if you don't turn up.

358
00:42:38,753 --> 00:42:40,753
I mean it, Kai.

359
00:42:40,821 --> 00:42:43,172
I promise.

360
00:42:51,716 --> 00:42:55,467
Wow, look at it.
It's beautiful.

361
00:42:55,536 --> 00:42:57,552
I'm getting in.

362
00:43:33,524 --> 00:43:35,391
<i> You know you want to.</i>

363
00:43:37,494 --> 00:43:39,979
<i> You know</i>
<i> you want to come.</i>

364
00:43:48,840 --> 00:43:50,673
Look at that.

365
00:43:50,742 --> 00:43:53,592
Oh, it goes so fast.

366
00:43:53,661 --> 00:43:56,495
This is neat.
Wow.

367
00:43:59,117 --> 00:44:01,216
Let's get out of here.

368
00:45:04,098 --> 00:45:07,032
I didn't want you
to see my new dress yet.

369
00:45:08,568 --> 00:45:10,402
What do you think?

370
00:45:11,622 --> 00:45:13,189
You're not ready.

371
00:45:13,257 --> 00:45:15,774
And what do you
have your skates for?

372
00:45:15,843 --> 00:45:20,813
Gerda, will you just keep these
for me till tomorrow?

373
00:45:20,881 --> 00:45:22,430
Why?

374
00:45:22,500 --> 00:45:24,850
Please, just do it.

375
00:45:33,361 --> 00:45:37,529
I'll see you downstairs
in five minutes.

376
00:46:15,419 --> 00:46:17,452
There she is.
Happy birthday, Gerda.

377
00:46:17,521 --> 00:46:20,588
Doesn't she
look lovely?

378
00:47:14,962 --> 00:47:17,329
He'll be here.

379
00:47:17,398 --> 00:47:21,066
He promised.

380
00:47:32,830 --> 00:47:35,130
<i> I've got</i>
<i> what you want, Kai.</i>

381
00:48:28,002 --> 00:48:29,567
Make a wish.

382
00:48:32,656 --> 00:48:35,824
<i> Kai... </i>

383
00:48:44,834 --> 00:48:46,568
Forget him.

384
00:48:46,637 --> 00:48:50,239
Something must be wrong.
I have to go look for him.

385
00:48:50,307 --> 00:48:53,042
Gerda, he's a foolish,
selfish boy.

386
00:48:53,110 --> 00:48:55,761
You deserve better.

387
00:48:55,830 --> 00:48:59,314
You don't know him at all.
None of you do.

388
00:48:59,383 --> 00:49:00,515
Gerda...

389
00:49:00,584 --> 00:49:04,102
No. Let her go.

390
00:50:18,428 --> 00:50:19,944
Hey, here,
let me have your sled.

391
00:50:20,013 --> 00:50:20,945
No.

392
00:50:21,014 --> 00:50:21,946
Just give it to me.

393
00:50:22,015 --> 00:50:23,081
No, I'm playing with it.

394
00:50:27,604 --> 00:50:31,473
Take me with you.

395
00:50:41,668 --> 00:50:43,151
Faster!

396
00:50:43,219 --> 00:50:45,753
How fast would you
like to go?

397
00:50:45,823 --> 00:50:47,589
As fast as you can go.

398
00:51:15,869 --> 00:51:17,702
Faster!

399
00:51:53,039 --> 00:51:55,741
I think
I've broken my arm.

400
00:51:55,809 --> 00:51:57,676
I don't think so.

401
00:51:59,980 --> 00:52:02,614
You know I told you
you wanted something from me,

402
00:52:02,683 --> 00:52:04,283
but you didn't know
what it was?

403
00:52:04,351 --> 00:52:07,518
This is what it was.

404
00:52:47,811 --> 00:52:52,080
It's all right, Kai.
You can hold on to me.

405
00:52:58,738 --> 00:53:02,574
See, they love the winter.
They embrace it.

406
00:53:10,650 --> 00:53:13,051
And up here,
they fear the winter,

407
00:53:13,119 --> 00:53:15,953
huddle away from it.

408
00:53:16,022 --> 00:53:17,472
Shall we teach them
a lesson?

409
00:53:18,809 --> 00:53:20,308
I think we shall.

410
00:53:33,807 --> 00:53:36,474
Isn't it marvelous?

411
00:53:36,543 --> 00:53:39,310
Doesn't it make your blood
just run cold with joy?

412
00:53:39,379 --> 00:53:41,412
I can't believe
you just did that.

413
00:53:41,481 --> 00:53:45,033
I can do anything I want.
That's the whole point.

414
00:53:54,378 --> 00:53:56,695
Slow down, girls.

415
00:54:11,878 --> 00:54:13,377
He always was
a reckless boy.

416
00:54:13,446 --> 00:54:16,081
You keep taking chances,
you pay the price in the end.

417
00:54:16,149 --> 00:54:19,016
That's the truth.
That's the cold, hard truth.

418
00:54:19,069 --> 00:54:21,052
He didn't die.
I know it.

419
00:54:21,121 --> 00:54:25,257
He was with that woman.
Somehow, she took him.

420
00:54:25,326 --> 00:54:27,225
Woman?
What woman?

421
00:54:27,294 --> 00:54:30,262
She stayed here
the night he disappeared.

422
00:54:30,331 --> 00:54:33,966
No, the pass was closed.
We didn't have any guests.

423
00:54:45,496 --> 00:54:47,862
I know how much
you miss him,

424
00:54:47,931 --> 00:54:52,067
but you must face the fact
that he is dead,

425
00:54:52,135 --> 00:54:54,352
and I know it doesn't
seem like it now,

426
00:54:54,421 --> 00:54:58,089
but you will come
to accept it over time.

427
00:54:58,158 --> 00:55:02,143
Like you did?

428
00:55:07,634 --> 00:55:09,000
Minna, when I talk
to my father

429
00:55:09,069 --> 00:55:11,136
about Kai's
disappearance,

430
00:55:11,205 --> 00:55:13,238
I can see something
hidden deep in his eyes,

431
00:55:13,307 --> 00:55:16,074
something he's
not telling me.

432
00:55:16,143 --> 00:55:20,345
I think you know
what it is.

433
00:55:20,413 --> 00:55:28,586
It's just that there have been
a lot of very unusual things

434
00:55:28,655 --> 00:55:31,522
going on in recent years,
unexplained things.

435
00:55:31,591 --> 00:55:34,059
You mean
like my mother's death?

436
00:55:34,128 --> 00:55:40,598
Yes, and many others,
who just... Disappeared.

437
00:55:42,302 --> 00:55:45,170
But, you know, maybe it's best
we don't talk about this.

438
00:55:45,238 --> 00:55:47,855
No, minna.
You have to tell me.

439
00:55:47,924 --> 00:55:49,657
Who were the people
who disappeared?

440
00:55:49,726 --> 00:55:54,896
Young men, mostly, boys,

441
00:55:54,965 --> 00:55:56,915
from villages

442
00:55:56,983 --> 00:55:58,750
all across the valley
and beyond,

443
00:55:58,819 --> 00:56:01,353
most of them disappearing
without a trace.

444
00:56:01,405 --> 00:56:03,271
But how?

445
00:56:03,340 --> 00:56:04,672
Why?

446
00:56:04,741 --> 00:56:07,692
Well, some think
they were taken, abducted.

447
00:56:07,761 --> 00:56:10,095
By whom?

448
00:56:10,163 --> 00:56:12,631
Tell me.

449
00:56:12,699 --> 00:56:15,500
The Snow Queen.

450
00:56:15,569 --> 00:56:17,519
You mean winter?

451
00:56:17,588 --> 00:56:19,237
No.

452
00:56:19,306 --> 00:56:22,206
Winter is merely
the Snow Queen's...

453
00:56:22,275 --> 00:56:25,176
Pet.

454
00:56:25,245 --> 00:56:29,047
But it's all
just a myth, child.

455
00:56:29,116 --> 00:56:30,581
Please promise me

456
00:56:30,650 --> 00:56:33,318
you won't concern yourself
with it.

457
00:56:59,546 --> 00:57:02,113
Brothers and sisters
in Christ,

458
00:57:02,181 --> 00:57:05,116
this morning we're gathered
to honor and remember

459
00:57:05,184 --> 00:57:07,869
the life of brother Kai

460
00:57:07,937 --> 00:57:12,056
and to celebrate the promise
of his sure resurrection.

461
00:57:12,125 --> 00:57:13,975
The Lord is my Shepherd...

462
00:57:14,044 --> 00:57:16,744
He makes me lie down
in green pastures.

463
00:57:16,813 --> 00:57:18,897
He leads me
beside quiet waters.

464
00:57:18,965 --> 00:57:22,550
He guides me in the paths
of righteousness for his
name's sake...

465
00:58:19,142 --> 00:58:21,876
Let me have him back.

466
00:58:24,214 --> 00:58:28,716
I'll give you my beautiful boots
if you let me have him back.

467
00:58:53,576 --> 00:58:56,645
I'll give you myself
for Kai.

468
01:00:08,150 --> 01:00:11,402
Come back,
little girl.

469
01:00:11,471 --> 01:00:15,340
You don't want to go yet.
You don't want to go.

470
01:00:19,379 --> 01:00:23,648
You're not dead, my little girl.
No, no, no.

471
01:00:23,716 --> 01:00:27,351
You are just full of water
inside of you.

472
01:00:27,420 --> 01:00:30,604
Come on, spit it out.
Come back.

473
01:00:30,673 --> 01:00:34,191
Come back!

474
01:00:43,403 --> 01:00:45,603
What were you doing
in the water?

475
01:00:45,672 --> 01:00:48,773
I threw myself in.

476
01:00:48,841 --> 01:00:51,842
Good thing I was
expecting you.

477
01:00:51,911 --> 01:00:56,748
Your boots arrived
a few minutes ago.

478
01:02:19,816 --> 01:02:21,433
Help yourself
to the strawberries.

479
01:02:21,501 --> 01:02:24,068
Watch out
for the juice, though.

480
01:02:24,136 --> 01:02:25,670
Remember
the last time,

481
01:02:25,739 --> 01:02:29,306
you couldn't get them
out of your dress?

482
01:02:29,376 --> 01:02:30,825
Threw yourself in,
did you?

483
01:02:32,362 --> 01:02:34,978
One of those quiet,
obedient girls

484
01:02:35,047 --> 01:02:37,615
who doesn't say anything
until she screams.

485
01:02:37,684 --> 01:02:39,717
Oh, the world's
full of them.

486
01:02:39,785 --> 01:02:41,385
"Sleepy girls,"
I call them.

487
01:02:41,454 --> 01:02:43,655
Sleepy girls...

488
01:02:44,991 --> 01:02:46,807
That when someone
combs your hair,

489
01:02:46,876 --> 01:02:49,210
you get sleepy?

490
01:02:49,278 --> 01:02:52,013
I can't stay here.

491
01:02:52,082 --> 01:02:53,848
I'm looking for someone.

492
01:02:53,916 --> 01:02:55,666
Lovely hair you've got.

493
01:02:55,735 --> 01:02:58,019
It's so long,

494
01:02:59,923 --> 01:03:02,523
and you must be
so tired.

495
01:03:02,592 --> 01:03:04,592
Beautiful...

496
01:03:04,661 --> 01:03:05,860
Lovely,

497
01:03:05,928 --> 01:03:09,130
sleepy hair.

498
01:03:09,199 --> 01:03:10,731
Dropping off.

499
01:03:10,800 --> 01:03:14,251
Very sleepy now.

500
01:03:21,895 --> 01:03:24,562
I can't stay here.

501
01:03:24,631 --> 01:03:26,247
I'm looking
for someone.

502
01:03:26,316 --> 01:03:29,450
Kai— have you
seen him?

503
01:03:29,519 --> 01:03:31,185
Please tell me
you've seen him.

504
01:03:31,254 --> 01:03:34,972
Kai, Kai, I'm sure
he'll pop by.

505
01:03:35,041 --> 01:03:37,308
In a minute, you'll decide
you want to go to sleep.

506
01:03:37,376 --> 01:03:40,578
I don't know
where he is,

507
01:03:40,647 --> 01:03:42,280
but I set off
to find him

508
01:03:42,348 --> 01:03:44,282
because I couldn't stand
doing nothing.

509
01:03:44,350 --> 01:03:48,102
Up to bed, then.
There's a good girl.

510
01:03:48,171 --> 01:03:50,071
No, I must go on.

511
01:03:50,139 --> 01:03:53,908
You must go back
before you can go on.

512
01:03:53,977 --> 01:03:54,909
No.

513
01:03:54,978 --> 01:03:57,745
Thank you
for rescuing me,

514
01:03:57,814 --> 01:03:59,747
but I have
to find Kai.

515
01:03:59,816 --> 01:04:01,148
I can't stay here.

516
01:04:01,217 --> 01:04:02,316
As you wish.

517
01:04:02,384 --> 01:04:04,351
It was nice of you
to stop by, anyway.

518
01:04:04,420 --> 01:04:08,656
Quite nice of me
to save your life, as well.

519
01:04:08,725 --> 01:04:12,627
You worry too much,
sleepy girl,

520
01:04:12,696 --> 01:04:14,629
who takes the weight
of the whole world

521
01:04:14,698 --> 01:04:15,997
on her shoulders,

522
01:04:16,066 --> 01:04:18,499
trying to grow up
too soon.

523
01:04:20,636 --> 01:04:24,589
How's the bed?
Is it by any chance

524
01:04:24,658 --> 01:04:26,691
the softest bed
you've ever been in?

525
01:04:30,763 --> 01:04:34,449
It's...
It's indescribable.

526
01:04:34,517 --> 01:04:38,169
Didn't have any
bedtime stories

527
01:04:38,238 --> 01:04:41,005
when we were
a little girl, did we?

528
01:04:41,074 --> 01:04:42,573
My poor old sausage.

529
01:04:42,642 --> 01:04:45,493
I'll make up for that,
I promise you.

530
01:04:47,563 --> 01:04:49,464
Gerda... Gerda.
Gerda, listen,

531
01:04:49,532 --> 01:04:50,865
roses?

532
01:04:50,933 --> 01:04:53,484
Is it that time
of year already?

533
01:04:55,271 --> 01:04:58,189
They remind me
of something, someone.

534
01:04:58,257 --> 01:05:00,641
Do they make you think
of a boy?

535
01:05:00,710 --> 01:05:02,910
<i> Gerda... </i>
<i> Kai needs you.</i>

536
01:05:02,979 --> 01:05:06,848
<i> We can help you find him.</i>
<i> We know where he is.</i>

537
01:05:06,916 --> 01:05:09,733
I think he needed help.
He needed someone to...

538
01:05:11,187 --> 01:05:13,221
Get out of here.

539
01:05:17,526 --> 01:05:20,611
Oh, it's so hard
to remember.

540
01:05:20,680 --> 01:05:23,981
You need to stop
trying so hard,

541
01:05:24,050 --> 01:05:25,349
don't you?

542
01:05:25,418 --> 01:05:29,053
Yes, I suppose I do.

543
01:05:29,122 --> 01:05:35,492
Now, go to sleep,
my sweetheart,

544
01:05:35,561 --> 01:05:37,228
just like mommy says.

545
01:05:45,238 --> 01:05:48,272
Gerda?

546
01:05:48,341 --> 01:05:51,158
Gerda,
time to get up.

547
01:05:57,617 --> 01:05:59,317
Wolfgang!

548
01:05:59,385 --> 01:06:01,285
Wolfgang!

549
01:09:29,995 --> 01:09:32,797
Lovely girl.

550
01:09:32,865 --> 01:09:34,865
Such a lovely girl,

551
01:09:34,934 --> 01:09:38,468
and you're such
lovely company.

552
01:09:38,537 --> 01:09:40,888
That's why I like you
so much.

553
01:09:40,957 --> 01:09:42,990
You're kind
and considerate,

554
01:09:43,059 --> 01:09:46,193
and you really help
around the house.

555
01:09:46,262 --> 01:09:47,928
You are a joy
to have around, really.

556
01:09:49,148 --> 01:09:51,632
Look at you smiling.

557
01:09:54,336 --> 01:09:56,336
You had to grow up
too soon, didn't you?

558
01:09:56,405 --> 01:09:59,640
It must have been awful.

559
01:09:59,708 --> 01:10:01,108
Yes, it was.

560
01:10:01,177 --> 01:10:03,961
You know the best time
in your life?

561
01:10:04,030 --> 01:10:05,195
It's when you're young

562
01:10:05,264 --> 01:10:07,448
and you've got someone
to take care of you

563
01:10:07,516 --> 01:10:08,982
night and day.

564
01:10:09,051 --> 01:10:11,936
It's what I call
"the spring of life."

565
01:10:43,052 --> 01:10:44,986
So you're up.

566
01:10:45,054 --> 01:10:47,370
Where am I?

567
01:10:47,439 --> 01:10:49,689
Where does it look
like you are?

568
01:10:49,758 --> 01:10:54,194
You're home, right down
to the last detail.

569
01:10:54,263 --> 01:10:57,114
How long have I
been asleep?

570
01:10:57,182 --> 01:10:59,733
I don't know.
I was away on business.

571
01:10:59,802 --> 01:11:01,102
A couple of months.

572
01:11:01,170 --> 01:11:03,720
Months?

573
01:11:03,789 --> 01:11:06,123
I'm home now,
home for the summer.

574
01:11:06,192 --> 01:11:08,558
I did my work
for the year.

575
01:11:08,627 --> 01:11:12,196
I can't stay here.

576
01:11:12,265 --> 01:11:13,864
It's too cold.

577
01:11:13,933 --> 01:11:18,836
Poor Kai.
All change involves pain.

578
01:11:18,904 --> 01:11:20,220
You don't understand.

579
01:11:20,289 --> 01:11:22,489
If I stay here,
I'm going to freeze to death.

580
01:11:22,558 --> 01:11:26,844
Well, then,
I suppose you'll die.

581
01:11:26,913 --> 01:11:30,864
I want a fire.
Just let me get some—

582
01:11:30,933 --> 01:11:32,165
no fire!

583
01:11:32,235 --> 01:11:34,368
No fire!

584
01:11:38,441 --> 01:11:41,408
I hate fire.

585
01:11:43,946 --> 01:11:46,614
Kai,

586
01:11:46,682 --> 01:11:49,883
answer me
one question.

587
01:11:49,952 --> 01:11:55,756
Have you ever
in your whole life

588
01:11:55,825 --> 01:11:58,392
ever felt anything like
that first kiss I gave you?

589
01:11:58,461 --> 01:12:00,494
No.

590
01:12:00,563 --> 01:12:01,662
No, you haven't.

591
01:12:05,934 --> 01:12:09,136
This...
This was once

592
01:12:09,204 --> 01:12:11,272
the most beautiful mirror
in the world.

593
01:12:13,842 --> 01:12:15,425
I'm sure an intelligent boy
like you

594
01:12:15,494 --> 01:12:17,427
could put it back together
quite easily.

595
01:12:17,496 --> 01:12:20,464
Once you've put it
back together,

596
01:12:20,533 --> 01:12:22,666
then you can go...

597
01:12:22,735 --> 01:12:25,369
If you still want to.

598
01:12:25,438 --> 01:12:28,872
I'm not going to do
anything you say,

599
01:12:28,941 --> 01:12:30,474
and I'm certainly

600
01:12:30,543 --> 01:12:33,710
not going to touch
some stupid glass jigsaw.

601
01:12:44,741 --> 01:12:47,274
You want to know
what real cold is?

602
01:12:52,281 --> 01:12:55,733
Real cold
will kill you dead,

603
01:12:55,801 --> 01:12:57,367
just like that.

604
01:12:57,436 --> 01:13:00,604
Stop it, please.

605
01:13:00,673 --> 01:13:04,558
You're to stay
on the ground floor.

606
01:13:04,626 --> 01:13:06,894
I'm a very
light sleeper,

607
01:13:06,963 --> 01:13:09,029
and if you wake me up
during the summer,

608
01:13:09,098 --> 01:13:15,002
I'll make you suffer.

609
01:13:17,690 --> 01:13:19,823
I kissed you once,

610
01:13:19,892 --> 01:13:21,458
and you slept
for two months.

611
01:13:21,527 --> 01:13:22,626
Think about that,

612
01:13:22,694 --> 01:13:25,445
because one kiss
won't last forever.

613
01:13:25,515 --> 01:13:26,947
Sooner or later,

614
01:13:27,016 --> 01:13:28,816
you're going to be
coming to me,

615
01:13:28,885 --> 01:13:30,818
begging me
for a second kiss.

616
01:13:30,887 --> 01:13:34,187
Why should I want
to kiss you again?

617
01:13:34,256 --> 01:13:36,390
I don't want
anything from you.

618
01:13:36,458 --> 01:13:39,827
That's what they all say...
To start with.

619
01:13:39,896 --> 01:13:41,862
I won't stay here.

620
01:13:41,930 --> 01:13:43,497
You're perfectly free
to leave, Kai,

621
01:13:43,565 --> 01:13:47,851
as soon as you
find a way out.

622
01:14:04,837 --> 01:14:07,271
Mommy, can I ask you
a question?

623
01:14:07,340 --> 01:14:10,107
Of course.

624
01:14:10,175 --> 01:14:12,976
When will I be old enough
to leave home?

625
01:14:13,045 --> 01:14:16,380
Why would you want
to leave home?

626
01:14:16,448 --> 01:14:19,316
What a horrible thing
to say.

627
01:14:19,385 --> 01:14:21,885
I'm sorry.
I just meant—

628
01:14:21,954 --> 01:14:23,254
no. No, no, no.

629
01:14:23,322 --> 01:14:27,758
You've really spoiled my day.
You've really upset me.

630
01:14:27,826 --> 01:14:29,726
Thank you so much

631
01:14:29,795 --> 01:14:34,280
for ruining years of happiness
with one unnecessary comment.

632
01:14:34,349 --> 01:14:37,517
Please tell me you're not
one of those selfish girls

633
01:14:37,586 --> 01:14:41,638
who only thinks
about what she wants.

634
01:14:41,707 --> 01:14:43,273
I'm sorry.

635
01:15:17,743 --> 01:15:19,660
I know you're not
really asleep.

636
01:15:21,847 --> 01:15:25,933
I'm not going to sit here
forever.

637
01:15:26,002 --> 01:15:27,901
Somebody's coming
to look for me.

638
01:15:27,970 --> 01:15:30,303
We're going to walk
out of here and go home.

639
01:15:30,372 --> 01:15:34,341
What do you think
about that?

640
01:15:58,100 --> 01:16:01,368
Afternoon nap for you,
my girl.

641
01:16:01,436 --> 01:16:05,139
Sleepy girl,
if I'm not mistaken.

642
01:16:05,207 --> 01:16:07,557
I was wondering...

643
01:16:07,627 --> 01:16:09,392
How long have I
been here for?

644
01:16:09,461 --> 01:16:13,930
What an extraordinary
question.

645
01:16:13,999 --> 01:16:16,166
You've been here
all your life.

646
01:16:18,804 --> 01:16:21,605
Sleepytime

647
01:16:21,674 --> 01:16:23,523
for sleepy girls.

648
01:16:23,592 --> 01:16:26,093
Time for
an afternoon nap.

649
01:16:26,161 --> 01:16:28,328
Time to get
your beauty sleep.

650
01:16:28,397 --> 01:16:32,632
There you go.
Off to bed.

651
01:16:32,701 --> 01:16:34,567
Sleepy girl...

652
01:17:27,189 --> 01:17:28,855
Gerda!

653
01:17:28,924 --> 01:17:31,208
Gerda!

654
01:17:31,277 --> 01:17:33,527
Oh, Wolfgang,
just let me catch my breath.

655
01:17:33,595 --> 01:17:35,645
Come on, minna.

656
01:17:35,714 --> 01:17:37,080
She must be here
somewhere.

657
01:17:37,149 --> 01:17:39,215
She knows these woods.
Gerda!

658
01:17:39,284 --> 01:17:40,383
All right.

659
01:18:02,107 --> 01:18:06,310
<i> Gerda... Gerda... </i>
<i> Over here.</i>

660
01:18:07,946 --> 01:18:11,682
Kai, you're here.
I know you're here.

661
01:18:15,253 --> 01:18:18,454
<i> Yes.</i>
<i> we can help you.</i>

662
01:18:18,523 --> 01:18:20,674
<i> We know where he is.</i>

663
01:18:23,629 --> 01:18:24,961
Kai?

664
01:18:25,030 --> 01:18:26,246
<i> Kai is not here.</i>

665
01:18:26,315 --> 01:18:27,648
Is Kai dead?

666
01:18:27,716 --> 01:18:29,950
<i> No.</i>
<i> we've been in the earth,</i>

667
01:18:30,018 --> 01:18:32,185
<i> where the dead are,</i>
<i> but Kai is not here.</i>

668
01:18:32,254 --> 01:18:35,122
<i> He passed here months ago.</i>
<i> He was with the Snow Queen.</i>

669
01:18:35,191 --> 01:18:37,157
But where
have they gone?

670
01:18:37,226 --> 01:18:39,576
<i> They are nowhere.</i>
<i> She is winter,</i>

671
01:18:39,644 --> 01:18:41,995
<i> and winter has passed.</i>
<i> Winter is elsewhere.</i>

672
01:18:42,064 --> 01:18:44,864
But she must have taken him
somewhere.

673
01:18:44,933 --> 01:18:46,616
Where did she go?

674
01:18:46,685 --> 01:18:49,453
<i> To her great place</i>
<i> in the north,</i>

675
01:18:49,521 --> 01:18:51,688
<i> if you want</i>
<i> to find Snow Queen,</i>

676
01:18:51,757 --> 01:18:53,907
<i> you must pass</i>
<i> through each season</i>

677
01:18:53,976 --> 01:18:56,576
<i> before you can reach her,</i>
<i> and unless you reach him</i>

678
01:18:56,662 --> 01:18:59,162
<i> before the winter solstice,</i>
<i> Kai will die there, too.</i>

679
01:18:59,231 --> 01:19:01,147
No!

680
01:19:08,490 --> 01:19:09,773
So you're going
to walk out

681
01:19:09,841 --> 01:19:13,210
into the darkness of the forest
all on your own,

682
01:19:13,279 --> 01:19:15,312
a little girl
with no food?

683
01:19:15,381 --> 01:19:17,063
I'm not a little girl,

684
01:19:17,132 --> 01:19:19,098
and I don't belong here.
You know that.

685
01:19:20,685 --> 01:19:22,235
You can't keep me here.
Let me go.

686
01:19:22,304 --> 01:19:24,421
You're right.
Why don't you just pop in,

687
01:19:24,490 --> 01:19:26,423
I'll make
a picnic, and—

688
01:19:26,492 --> 01:19:28,492
no.

689
01:19:28,561 --> 01:19:30,677
If I go back in,
you will never let me out.

690
01:19:30,745 --> 01:19:32,779
You'll see to that.

691
01:19:32,847 --> 01:19:35,315
What are you going to do
when you find the Snow Queen?

692
01:19:35,384 --> 01:19:37,984
You can't defeat her.
It's hopeless.

693
01:19:38,053 --> 01:19:39,385
How do you know?

694
01:19:39,454 --> 01:19:42,406
Because...

695
01:19:42,474 --> 01:19:44,541
Because she's my sister.

696
01:19:44,609 --> 01:19:48,195
It's true, Gerda,

697
01:19:48,263 --> 01:19:49,947
and only I know

698
01:19:50,015 --> 01:19:54,051
how truly cold and ruthless
she is at her core.

699
01:19:54,119 --> 01:19:56,703
I've watched her
year after year

700
01:19:56,772 --> 01:19:59,706
clawing
for more power.

701
01:19:59,774 --> 01:20:01,875
Her arrogance
knows no bounds.

702
01:20:01,944 --> 01:20:05,312
However hopeless it is,
I must find him.

703
01:20:05,380 --> 01:20:09,266
But why?
Why is he worth it?

704
01:20:09,334 --> 01:20:13,937
Because he made me
want to live again.

705
01:20:16,992 --> 01:20:20,377
Remember
how I saved you?

706
01:20:20,446 --> 01:20:24,581
Never underestimate
the power of a kiss.

707
01:24:32,381 --> 01:24:34,865
Gerda!

708
01:24:34,933 --> 01:24:37,367
Gerda!

709
01:24:37,435 --> 01:24:40,603
Gerda!

710
01:24:41,656 --> 01:24:43,256
Gerda!

711
01:24:44,526 --> 01:24:45,758
No, no.

712
01:24:47,862 --> 01:24:50,030
It's just a log,
Wolfgang.

713
01:24:50,098 --> 01:24:51,798
It's only a log.

714
01:24:57,338 --> 01:25:00,357
It's all right.
We'll find her.

715
01:25:00,425 --> 01:25:02,959
I know in my heart
she's going to be fine.

716
01:25:03,027 --> 01:25:06,112
I hope...

717
01:26:49,084 --> 01:26:53,286
Since you seem to have
forgotten the hotel rules,

718
01:26:53,354 --> 01:26:55,922
I'll run through
them for you.

719
01:26:55,991 --> 01:26:59,992
Rule one, never disturb
a sleeping polar bear,

720
01:27:00,061 --> 01:27:01,594
or you'll
get a smack.

721
01:27:01,663 --> 01:27:06,433
Rule two, if a polar bear
is not sleeping,

722
01:27:06,501 --> 01:27:08,251
he's almost
certainly fishing.

723
01:27:08,319 --> 01:27:11,871
If you disturb
a fishing polar bear,

724
01:27:11,939 --> 01:27:15,508
you will get a smack.
Rule three,

725
01:27:15,577 --> 01:27:19,478
any attempts at escape
will result in a smack.

726
01:27:19,547 --> 01:27:20,580
You got that, Sonny?

727
01:27:20,649 --> 01:27:22,381
Absolutely.

728
01:27:22,450 --> 01:27:23,650
Good.

729
01:27:35,097 --> 01:27:36,863
You really hit me.

730
01:27:36,932 --> 01:27:40,583
If I'd really hit you,
you'd be dead.

731
01:28:25,997 --> 01:28:28,314
Help! Help!

732
01:28:28,382 --> 01:28:30,600
Please to open the door...
Somebody...

733
01:28:30,668 --> 01:28:32,469
Who's in there?

734
01:28:32,537 --> 01:28:35,472
Hapless magician
needing urgent assistance.

735
01:28:35,540 --> 01:28:37,540
But you're
not in there!

736
01:28:37,609 --> 01:28:39,075
Definitely in here.

737
01:28:39,144 --> 01:28:41,711
Box is disappearing-
type cabinet...

738
01:28:41,779 --> 01:28:43,746
Hapless magician
inside.

739
01:28:43,815 --> 01:28:47,984
Please knock
on all surfaces.

740
01:28:48,052 --> 01:28:49,819
Harder!

741
01:28:49,887 --> 01:28:53,022
Harder!

742
01:28:53,091 --> 01:28:54,056
Aha!

743
01:28:54,126 --> 01:28:56,742
Endless thanks,
kind lady.

744
01:28:56,811 --> 01:28:58,511
Chen at your
service.

745
01:28:58,580 --> 01:29:01,347
My name's Gerda.
What are you doing here?

746
01:29:01,416 --> 01:29:04,067
Making way to gorgeous palace
of Summer Princess

747
01:29:04,135 --> 01:29:05,918
full of optimism
for post

748
01:29:05,987 --> 01:29:08,888
of conjuring entertainer
for royal court.

749
01:29:08,957 --> 01:29:10,757
Are you sure
you're ready for that?

750
01:29:10,825 --> 01:29:14,811
You seem a little uncomfortable
with the practical side.

751
01:29:14,879 --> 01:29:18,013
Chen therefore needing
beautiful and smart assistant.

752
01:29:18,082 --> 01:29:19,949
Well, I hope
you find one.

753
01:29:20,018 --> 01:29:23,019
No, no, no! Already found!
You she.

754
01:29:23,088 --> 01:29:25,638
You help Chen get job
in summer palace.

755
01:29:25,707 --> 01:29:27,040
I'd like to help you,

756
01:29:27,108 --> 01:29:28,708
but I have to save Kai
from the Snow Queen

757
01:29:28,777 --> 01:29:30,043
before
the winter solstice.

758
01:29:30,111 --> 01:29:32,762
Ah, Kai...
From Snow Queen...

759
01:29:34,032 --> 01:29:35,331
Do you know
where Snow Queen is?

760
01:29:35,400 --> 01:29:37,500
Not exactly, but i'm
not going to stop looking

761
01:29:37,569 --> 01:29:40,002
till I've found her.

762
01:29:40,071 --> 01:29:42,105
Summer Princess will know.
Snow Queen...

763
01:29:42,174 --> 01:29:45,825
Summer Princess...
Relations, got to be.

764
01:29:45,893 --> 01:29:48,427
You help Chen find
Summer Princess

765
01:29:48,496 --> 01:29:51,097
Summer Princess
help you find Kai.

766
01:29:51,165 --> 01:29:52,298
Good deal?

767
01:29:58,857 --> 01:29:59,922
Hmm...

768
01:30:00,859 --> 01:30:02,658
This is impossible.

769
01:30:02,727 --> 01:30:04,427
Get back to work.

770
01:30:04,495 --> 01:30:06,245
Don't you ever
want to get out of here?

771
01:30:06,314 --> 01:30:07,630
Why should I?

772
01:30:07,699 --> 01:30:09,365
This is
a very good fishing spot,

773
01:30:09,433 --> 01:30:14,320
I have a nice, cold,
north-facing room,

774
01:30:14,389 --> 01:30:15,621
and...

775
01:30:19,528 --> 01:30:20,727
And?

776
01:30:20,796 --> 01:30:23,279
And nothing.
Get back to work.

777
01:30:26,034 --> 01:30:27,567
All right.

778
01:30:27,636 --> 01:30:30,937
This is a very stupid
way to fish.

779
01:30:31,005 --> 01:30:33,222
I can't believe
you ever caught anything.

780
01:30:33,291 --> 01:30:36,826
I'm glad my father's
not here to see this.

781
01:30:36,895 --> 01:30:40,696
Humph— four hours
without a fish.

782
01:30:40,765 --> 01:30:42,548
Umm-umm-umm.

783
01:30:43,485 --> 01:30:46,051
Oh what a waste...

784
01:30:54,496 --> 01:30:57,163
And you are
looking for...?

785
01:30:58,516 --> 01:31:01,367
The way out.

786
01:31:01,436 --> 01:31:04,036
Why shouldn't I?
I don't want to be here.

787
01:31:04,105 --> 01:31:06,389
You haven't finished
the puzzle yet.

788
01:31:06,458 --> 01:31:08,241
I don't care about the puzzle.
I want to find Gerda.

789
01:31:08,310 --> 01:31:11,310
Her majesty wants you
to finish the puzzle,

790
01:31:11,379 --> 01:31:13,545
and I'm here
to make sure you do.

791
01:31:13,614 --> 01:31:15,498
Don't you have
a will of your own?

792
01:31:15,567 --> 01:31:16,566
Yes.

793
01:31:16,634 --> 01:31:18,701
It's to do
whatever she wants.

794
01:31:18,770 --> 01:31:20,420
What about what I want?

795
01:31:20,488 --> 01:31:23,640
Not really important.

796
01:31:33,902 --> 01:31:35,284
Ha ha!

797
01:31:35,353 --> 01:31:36,519
Told you.

798
01:31:36,587 --> 01:31:39,138
My way is better.

799
01:31:43,261 --> 01:31:45,144
What are you
looking at?

800
01:31:45,213 --> 01:31:47,313
Get back to work.

801
01:31:58,860 --> 01:32:01,144
I've made you
a nice dinner.

802
01:32:02,781 --> 01:32:05,732
Come, now, Wolfgang...

803
01:32:08,836 --> 01:32:11,070
You really must eat.

804
01:32:11,139 --> 01:32:13,439
It's your
favorite dish.

805
01:32:32,677 --> 01:32:35,311
I...

806
01:32:35,379 --> 01:32:37,246
I appreciate

807
01:32:37,315 --> 01:32:40,433
what you are
trying to do, minna,

808
01:32:40,502 --> 01:32:42,918
but I don't play...

809
01:32:44,639 --> 01:32:47,239
Anymore.

810
01:32:53,614 --> 01:32:55,782
Have you been traveling
a long way, Chen?

811
01:32:55,850 --> 01:32:58,150
Oh, very far.
All available palaces,

812
01:32:58,219 --> 01:33:00,019
all turning Chen down.

813
01:33:00,087 --> 01:33:02,422
You must practice very hard
to become a good magician.

814
01:33:02,490 --> 01:33:04,540
Problem
with practice,

815
01:33:04,608 --> 01:33:06,108
Chen always
getting self stuck.

816
01:33:06,177 --> 01:33:09,645
That's why young magician
so glad to find you.

817
01:33:13,851 --> 01:33:16,068
Chen taking this place
by storm.

818
01:33:16,137 --> 01:33:18,620
It looks very grand.

819
01:33:25,579 --> 01:33:27,646
<i> Kai... </i>

820
01:33:33,821 --> 01:33:35,922
Hello, Kai.

821
01:33:35,990 --> 01:33:39,225
How are you
settling in?

822
01:33:39,294 --> 01:33:42,228
Fine, thank you.

823
01:33:42,297 --> 01:33:44,931
Well, that's
certainly progress,

824
01:33:44,999 --> 01:33:46,532
considering
the last time we talked,

825
01:33:46,600 --> 01:33:48,467
you were cold
and miserable,

826
01:33:48,536 --> 01:33:51,387
and wanted nothing more
than to go home.

827
01:33:51,455 --> 01:33:55,240
How are you getting on
with my mirror?

828
01:33:55,310 --> 01:33:57,342
Quite well.

829
01:33:57,411 --> 01:34:00,713
Do you call that
"doing well," Kai?

830
01:34:01,983 --> 01:34:03,749
No, ma'am.

831
01:34:03,818 --> 01:34:06,669
What was that?
I didn't quite hear you.

832
01:34:06,738 --> 01:34:10,139
No, ma'am.

833
01:34:10,207 --> 01:34:12,008
It's hard.

834
01:34:12,076 --> 01:34:13,625
Hard?

835
01:34:23,204 --> 01:34:24,687
Too difficult, Kai?

836
01:34:28,926 --> 01:34:30,977
No.

837
01:34:31,045 --> 01:34:32,344
I should have
tried harder.

838
01:34:32,413 --> 01:34:34,263
Yes, you should.

839
01:34:35,883 --> 01:34:38,301
So, how should
I punish you

840
01:34:38,369 --> 01:34:40,669
for not trying
hard enough?

841
01:34:41,572 --> 01:34:43,673
I'm not your prisoner.

842
01:34:51,832 --> 01:34:54,000
Come here.

843
01:35:02,176 --> 01:35:05,494
Don't make me
tell you again.

844
01:35:19,260 --> 01:35:20,893
Does that hurt?

845
01:35:20,961 --> 01:35:23,362
What do you think?

846
01:35:31,889 --> 01:35:34,790
Does it hurt now?

847
01:35:36,327 --> 01:35:38,260
No.

848
01:35:41,265 --> 01:35:44,266
Have you
missed me, Kai?

849
01:35:44,335 --> 01:35:47,236
I've missed you
terribly.

850
01:35:47,305 --> 01:35:49,805
Have you thought
about me at all,

851
01:35:49,873 --> 01:35:53,475
or has your mind
been on that girl?

852
01:35:53,544 --> 01:35:57,180
Yes...

853
01:35:57,248 --> 01:35:58,581
I mean, no.

854
01:35:58,650 --> 01:36:02,951
I mean— I don't know
what I mean.

855
01:36:04,389 --> 01:36:06,822
Your hand's
shaking.

856
01:36:06,891 --> 01:36:08,824
Why's that?

857
01:36:11,563 --> 01:36:14,230
I guess it's been
a while, hasn't it,

858
01:36:14,299 --> 01:36:16,365
since I last
kissed you.

859
01:36:18,202 --> 01:36:19,868
You'd better get busy
on that mirror, Kai,

860
01:36:19,937 --> 01:36:22,871
because what you're
feeling now is nothing,

861
01:36:22,940 --> 01:36:24,173
trust me.

862
01:36:26,961 --> 01:36:33,432
Before long, you'll be
climbing those stairs,

863
01:36:33,500 --> 01:36:35,668
desperate
for another kiss.

864
01:37:29,306 --> 01:37:30,606
Couldn't we just
tell them we're here

865
01:37:30,675 --> 01:37:32,541
and ask for
an audition?

866
01:37:32,610 --> 01:37:35,945
Truth is, Chen already
auditioned at summer palace.

867
01:37:36,013 --> 01:37:38,263
Thrown out two,
three times.

868
01:37:38,332 --> 01:37:39,965
Only trying again

869
01:37:40,034 --> 01:37:42,868
because of smart
and beautiful assistant.

870
01:37:48,809 --> 01:37:50,909
When Summer Princess
comes down in the morning,

871
01:37:50,978 --> 01:37:52,377
we are amazing her

872
01:37:52,447 --> 01:37:53,896
before she's
throwing us out.

873
01:37:53,965 --> 01:37:55,564
I'm not sure

874
01:37:55,633 --> 01:37:57,499
how good of an idea
this is, Chen...

875
01:38:05,326 --> 01:38:06,358
Are they ghosts?

876
01:38:06,427 --> 01:38:08,794
No, no, just dreams.

877
01:38:08,863 --> 01:38:10,395
Dreams?

878
01:38:10,464 --> 01:38:13,666
Royal dreams.
None of our business.

879
01:38:13,734 --> 01:38:15,084
Please help find
magic deck of cards.

880
01:38:25,696 --> 01:38:26,995
Roses...

881
01:38:27,064 --> 01:38:29,681
Roses,
talk to me about Kai.

882
01:39:07,288 --> 01:39:08,988
Me...

883
01:39:09,056 --> 01:39:10,555
That's me.

884
01:39:13,344 --> 01:39:15,060
Intruders...

885
01:39:15,129 --> 01:39:16,829
Intruders!

886
01:39:16,898 --> 01:39:19,014
Not intruders!
Chinese magician,

887
01:39:19,083 --> 01:39:21,249
and smart and beautiful
assistant.

888
01:39:21,319 --> 01:39:22,351
You again.

889
01:39:22,419 --> 01:39:24,286
This time
with complete new show,

890
01:39:24,355 --> 01:39:25,888
all tricks at
highest perfection,

891
01:39:25,956 --> 01:39:28,373
and best
available back-up.

892
01:39:29,610 --> 01:39:31,027
We do audition now?

893
01:39:31,095 --> 01:39:32,011
Grab the
intruders!

894
01:39:32,080 --> 01:39:35,247
No! Entertainers,
for royal audition.

895
01:39:35,316 --> 01:39:36,665
Royal audition,
my foot.

896
01:39:36,734 --> 01:39:38,567
We've thrown you out
three times this summer!

897
01:39:38,635 --> 01:39:41,403
You! It's you!

898
01:39:41,472 --> 01:39:44,572
I'm very sorry, your highness.
I know we shouldn't be here,

899
01:39:44,641 --> 01:39:47,276
but I was wondering
if you could tell me—

900
01:39:47,328 --> 01:39:50,980
I've been dreaming about you
for months now!

901
01:39:51,049 --> 01:39:52,464
What shall I do with them,
your highness?

902
01:39:52,533 --> 01:39:53,933
Do with them?

903
01:39:54,001 --> 01:39:56,401
Why, give them
everything they want.

904
01:39:56,470 --> 01:39:59,455
Including the conjurer,
your highness?

905
01:40:02,877 --> 01:40:04,877
Oh, yes, he's been
very helpful.

906
01:40:04,946 --> 01:40:06,879
Then the conjurer too.

907
01:40:06,947 --> 01:40:08,463
You will not regretting this,
your highness.

908
01:40:08,532 --> 01:40:12,834
Chen soon delighting court
with all his tricks.

909
01:41:06,106 --> 01:41:10,409
Nosy boys tend not to live
too long around here.

910
01:41:18,369 --> 01:41:19,919
Best news ever!

911
01:41:19,987 --> 01:41:21,754
Princess letting Chen do
magic show without audition,

912
01:41:21,822 --> 01:41:22,988
thanks to you.

913
01:41:23,056 --> 01:41:24,673
Chen, that's wonderful,

914
01:41:26,059 --> 01:41:29,094
she has promised to tell the way
to the Snow Queen's palace.

915
01:41:30,731 --> 01:41:33,431
All I have to do is agree to
attend some ball she's giving.

916
01:41:33,500 --> 01:41:35,400
Perfect. That's where Chen
is putting on show.

917
01:41:46,747 --> 01:41:48,547
What are you
thinking about?

918
01:41:48,616 --> 01:41:49,682
Nothing.

919
01:41:49,750 --> 01:41:52,117
Come on,
you can tell me.

920
01:41:57,274 --> 01:41:59,124
Do you mind if I go
into the luggage room
to look for something?

921
01:41:59,193 --> 01:42:01,627
There is no way out
from there.

922
01:42:03,247 --> 01:42:04,879
I'm not looking
for a way out.

923
01:42:04,948 --> 01:42:06,014
I just want
to find something.

924
01:42:06,083 --> 01:42:07,382
What?

925
01:42:07,451 --> 01:42:10,352
You'll see.

926
01:42:30,992 --> 01:42:32,290
Here we are.

927
01:42:46,757 --> 01:42:50,059
The peasant look
is so last year, darling.

928
01:42:50,127 --> 01:42:51,709
It's light,
classic fabrics

929
01:42:51,778 --> 01:42:53,211
and heavy jewels
at the moment.

930
01:42:53,280 --> 01:42:55,647
A lot of money and plenty
of weight on fingers and face.

931
01:42:55,715 --> 01:42:57,483
Look in the mirror,
pumpkin.

932
01:42:57,551 --> 01:43:00,986
Mirrors don't lie.
Tell me what you see.

933
01:43:01,055 --> 01:43:02,771
I don't know.

934
01:43:02,840 --> 01:43:04,823
Nobody special.

935
01:43:04,892 --> 01:43:06,125
Yes...

936
01:43:06,193 --> 01:43:09,327
Well, that's what we're
going to change, darling.

937
01:43:10,831 --> 01:43:12,531
Promise me one
thing, poppet.

938
01:43:12,600 --> 01:43:14,733
Just don't leave
the grounds.

939
01:43:14,802 --> 01:43:17,102
The woods are full
of the most terrible robbers;

940
01:43:17,171 --> 01:43:21,407
I'd hate to see you become
yet another unfortunate victim.

941
01:43:21,475 --> 01:43:25,344
Do I look a porker
in this dress?

942
01:43:25,413 --> 01:43:27,413
I haven't got
time to change.

943
01:43:27,481 --> 01:43:30,216
We have such
a full day ahead of us.

944
01:43:31,885 --> 01:43:34,186
What are those men
doing outside?

945
01:43:34,255 --> 01:43:36,121
They're queuing
for tickets, darling.

946
01:43:36,190 --> 01:43:39,924
It's the engagement ball,
the biggest night of the summer.

947
01:43:39,993 --> 01:43:41,960
All the eligible bachelors
will be there,

948
01:43:42,029 --> 01:43:44,113
and if we're going
to get you married,

949
01:43:44,181 --> 01:43:46,948
we have to make you
absolutely beautiful.

950
01:43:47,017 --> 01:43:48,517
Married?

951
01:43:49,753 --> 01:43:51,153
But I don't want
to be married.

952
01:43:51,221 --> 01:43:53,539
I've told you,
I'm looking for Kai.

953
01:43:53,607 --> 01:43:56,408
And I promised to tell you
where to find him,

954
01:43:56,477 --> 01:43:59,611
but first you have
to check out the field,

955
01:43:59,680 --> 01:44:02,514
to see how many wonderful
young men are waiting for you.

956
01:44:02,583 --> 01:44:05,884
But, Princess,
it's Kai I love.

957
01:44:05,953 --> 01:44:07,085
Only Kai.

958
01:44:07,154 --> 01:44:08,904
Oh, yes.

959
01:44:08,973 --> 01:44:11,974
That cute, coy thing you do—
that "little girl lost" look,

960
01:44:12,043 --> 01:44:14,343
keep that.
It's very provocative.

961
01:44:14,411 --> 01:44:16,295
You'll have
the men drooling.

962
01:44:16,363 --> 01:44:18,163
"What a peach,
what a catch."

963
01:44:18,232 --> 01:44:20,982
Trust me
on this one.

964
01:44:21,051 --> 01:44:23,686
You'll be engaged
before midnight.

965
01:44:27,091 --> 01:44:28,523
Just a minute!

966
01:44:28,592 --> 01:44:31,459
Just a minute.

967
01:44:34,065 --> 01:44:36,932
Wolfgang,
come downstairs.

968
01:44:37,000 --> 01:44:38,367
You've got guests
to be seen to.

969
01:44:38,436 --> 01:44:40,419
Why should I care,
minna?

970
01:44:40,488 --> 01:44:43,005
Because you've got
a hotel to run,

971
01:44:43,074 --> 01:44:45,841
and it's the best hotel in town.
Now, come on.

972
01:44:45,909 --> 01:44:47,426
What's the point?

973
01:44:47,495 --> 01:44:49,378
The point is...

974
01:44:49,447 --> 01:44:55,016
The point is,
it's over, old friend.

975
01:44:55,085 --> 01:44:57,385
The point is,

976
01:44:57,454 --> 01:45:00,038
I barely have the strength
to live anymore.

977
01:45:17,191 --> 01:45:20,159
I can stand upright,
but that's about it.

978
01:45:21,711 --> 01:45:23,729
All right, come on,
lean forward.

979
01:45:27,751 --> 01:45:30,018
You have to lean
on one side of the skate.

980
01:45:30,086 --> 01:45:33,705
Polar bears
don't do a lot of leaning.

981
01:45:33,774 --> 01:45:35,841
Whoa!

982
01:45:35,909 --> 01:45:37,008
Easy, I got you.

983
01:45:37,077 --> 01:45:40,111
All right. Just try it.
Push forward.

984
01:45:40,180 --> 01:45:44,149
Can you go a little faster?
Try to go a little faster.

985
01:45:46,620 --> 01:45:49,588
Hey, I think I'm getting
the hang of it.

986
01:45:52,108 --> 01:45:53,542
Watch this.

987
01:45:53,611 --> 01:45:54,676
Easy!

988
01:46:47,815 --> 01:46:49,047
Hello,

989
01:46:49,116 --> 01:46:50,765
my name is Reginald.

990
01:46:52,385 --> 01:46:56,638
I have an excellent pedigree,
and several university diplomas.

991
01:46:56,706 --> 01:47:00,025
One of them is in dancing.
May I show you a few steps?

992
01:47:18,378 --> 01:47:19,894
Summa cum laude
in the waltz...

993
01:47:26,086 --> 01:47:28,586
And honorable mention
in the flamenco.

994
01:47:51,512 --> 01:47:53,578
My other diplomas

995
01:47:53,647 --> 01:47:56,214
include horsemanship,
sportsmanship...

996
01:47:58,018 --> 01:48:00,802
And awfully
nice manners.

997
01:48:03,741 --> 01:48:07,609
Oh, dear.
I thought he was your type.

998
01:48:07,677 --> 01:48:09,211
Very nice
cheekbones,

999
01:48:09,279 --> 01:48:10,678
and all those
diplomas...

1000
01:48:10,748 --> 01:48:13,381
But, Princess, I'm really
not looking for anybody,

1001
01:48:13,450 --> 01:48:16,334
no, of course.
You're a shy girl, aren't you?

1002
01:48:16,403 --> 01:48:18,286
Except that
shy girls

1003
01:48:18,355 --> 01:48:20,088
don't break into
palaces at night,

1004
01:48:20,157 --> 01:48:24,026
do they?
With wandering conjurers, hmm?

1005
01:48:25,195 --> 01:48:27,629
Oh— things
are looking up!

1006
01:48:27,698 --> 01:48:30,031
Eyes left, coming
straight towards us.

1007
01:48:30,100 --> 01:48:32,333
Get a load
of the dimples on this one.

1008
01:48:32,403 --> 01:48:36,471
Major delfont chalfont,
at your service.

1009
01:48:36,540 --> 01:48:39,557
I'd lay down my life
if your honor was at stake.

1010
01:48:39,626 --> 01:48:41,476
Would you like
to dance?

1011
01:48:45,215 --> 01:48:47,616
Thank you, but I'm really
not a dancer.

1012
01:48:47,685 --> 01:48:49,918
Neither am I, my darling,
but, do you know,

1013
01:48:49,987 --> 01:48:54,056
I like to put on
a rather good show.

1014
01:49:13,109 --> 01:49:14,976
Did I ever tell you
all about my exploits

1015
01:49:15,044 --> 01:49:18,112
with the 35th horse brigade
at the battle of tompkins bay?

1016
01:49:18,181 --> 01:49:20,482
You couldn't have.
We've only just met.

1017
01:49:22,235 --> 01:49:24,936
We were absolutely
surrounded, you know,

1018
01:49:25,005 --> 01:49:27,039
on all sides,

1019
01:49:27,107 --> 01:49:29,357
by these strapping
circassian warriors.

1020
01:49:29,425 --> 01:49:32,093
Great scimitars
flashing.

1021
01:49:32,162 --> 01:49:34,796
There was a cannon
to the left of us,

1022
01:49:34,865 --> 01:49:37,198
a cannon also
to the right of us.

1023
01:49:37,267 --> 01:49:38,466
Do you know what
my colonel said,

1024
01:49:38,535 --> 01:49:40,384
when he walked up
to me?

1025
01:49:40,453 --> 01:49:41,385
One of the most
amusing anecdotes

1026
01:49:41,454 --> 01:49:42,688
I think
I've ever heard...

1027
01:50:07,447 --> 01:50:09,447
How big
is this place?

1028
01:50:09,516 --> 01:50:11,533
As big as you
want it to be.

1029
01:50:20,110 --> 01:50:22,176
I think you've got
natural ability.

1030
01:50:22,245 --> 01:50:23,712
Do you really?

1031
01:50:23,781 --> 01:50:27,081
Or are you just buttering me up
before trying to escape again?

1032
01:50:27,150 --> 01:50:29,017
No, I'm simply
having fun.

1033
01:50:29,085 --> 01:50:31,219
All right,

1034
01:50:31,288 --> 01:50:34,122
as long as it's
just that.

1035
01:50:40,714 --> 01:50:43,849
I wouldn't be surprised
if she kissed me again tonight.

1036
01:50:47,404 --> 01:50:49,120
Let go, I didn't mean it!
I'm sorry!

1037
01:50:49,189 --> 01:50:50,789
I can't breathe!

1038
01:50:56,813 --> 01:50:59,380
You're in love with her
yourself, aren't you?

1039
01:51:01,735 --> 01:51:04,035
Just let me go.

1040
01:51:04,104 --> 01:51:06,437
Then it'd just be
you and her.

1041
01:51:09,309 --> 01:51:14,745
Please let me go.
I'm not meant to be here.

1042
01:51:14,814 --> 01:51:16,847
No.

1043
01:51:16,916 --> 01:51:20,519
I'm not going to hold out
much longer.

1044
01:51:20,587 --> 01:51:21,686
Please let me go home.

1045
01:51:21,755 --> 01:51:24,339
No.
No... no!

1046
01:51:24,408 --> 01:51:29,427
Why are you so angry?
Is it because you're in pain?

1047
01:51:33,967 --> 01:51:35,100
How long have you
been in pain?

1048
01:51:35,169 --> 01:51:37,485
Let me guess.

1049
01:51:37,553 --> 01:51:40,321
Since you met her,
perhaps?

1050
01:51:49,449 --> 01:51:52,150
I've been watching you
all evening, my darling,

1051
01:51:52,219 --> 01:51:54,519
and I'm head over heels
in love with you.

1052
01:51:54,588 --> 01:51:56,587
They call me
"handsome Helmut."

1053
01:51:56,657 --> 01:51:58,607
I'm sorry, Helmut,
I'm not in the mood for—

1054
01:51:58,675 --> 01:52:00,475
would you look at my profile
just for a moment?

1055
01:52:00,544 --> 01:52:02,777
Paying particular
attention to the angle

1056
01:52:02,845 --> 01:52:04,112
at which my nose
relates to my forehead.

1057
01:52:04,181 --> 01:52:06,214
Yes, they go together
very well.

1058
01:52:06,283 --> 01:52:09,250
Is that all
you have to say?

1059
01:52:09,319 --> 01:52:13,371
Are you aware that young ladies
generally lose consciousness

1060
01:52:13,423 --> 01:52:15,790
perhaps
they do, Helmut,

1061
01:52:15,859 --> 01:52:18,877
but I, for some reason,
am able to resist it.

1062
01:52:22,532 --> 01:52:24,982
She's not showing interest
in any of the men.

1063
01:52:25,051 --> 01:52:29,587
If she doesn't fall in love,
summer will come to an end.

1064
01:52:29,656 --> 01:52:31,623
Count rothstein,
go to her,

1065
01:52:31,691 --> 01:52:33,824
don't come back until
she's fallen in love with you.

1066
01:52:33,893 --> 01:52:37,795
I've tried twice already.
She just looks the other way.

1067
01:52:37,864 --> 01:52:42,634
All right.
This calls for real firepower.

1068
01:52:42,702 --> 01:52:44,936
Send in Charles D'Amour.

1069
01:52:45,005 --> 01:52:46,104
Charles D'Amour?

1070
01:52:46,172 --> 01:52:47,588
If anyone
can make her forget

1071
01:52:47,657 --> 01:52:49,925
about this silly little boy
she's doting on,

1072
01:52:49,993 --> 01:52:52,827
it's Charles D'Amour.

1073
01:52:52,896 --> 01:52:56,464
Come on.
Let's find him.

1074
01:53:00,337 --> 01:53:01,953
You leave me
no choice.

1075
01:53:02,021 --> 01:53:03,521
I'm going to
kill myself

1076
01:53:03,590 --> 01:53:05,423
unless you agree to marry me
this very moment.

1077
01:53:05,492 --> 01:53:06,941
Helmut...

1078
01:53:07,009 --> 01:53:09,678
That's it. It's over.
Hold these, would you?

1079
01:53:17,804 --> 01:53:19,253
I am...

1080
01:53:19,322 --> 01:53:22,857
Charles D'Amour,
Prince of Burgundy.

1081
01:53:22,926 --> 01:53:27,545
I have ridden bareback
from France to find beauty.

1082
01:53:27,614 --> 01:53:31,666
<i> Mon amour,</i>
<i> </i> my search is over.

1083
01:53:44,297 --> 01:53:45,430
<i> Enchante.</i>

1084
01:53:47,017 --> 01:53:48,633
Who are you?

1085
01:53:48,701 --> 01:53:51,369
I'm Chen the magician,
and lady has vanished.

1086
01:53:51,438 --> 01:53:53,137
Why, you little...

1087
01:53:53,206 --> 01:53:56,174
Conjurer has also vanished.
Good night.

1088
01:54:10,106 --> 01:54:12,640
Kai...

1089
01:54:12,709 --> 01:54:16,577
What's the word
to describe you?

1090
01:54:16,646 --> 01:54:18,663
Willful.

1091
01:54:20,600 --> 01:54:22,967
Willful would be
a good word.

1092
01:54:23,036 --> 01:54:24,769
You're testing
my patience.

1093
01:54:24,837 --> 01:54:29,623
I've been working really hard.
I just needed a break.

1094
01:54:29,692 --> 01:54:31,125
I mean,
I can't work forever.

1095
01:54:31,194 --> 01:54:33,979
Do you know what I think
the problem is?

1096
01:54:34,047 --> 01:54:35,847
Your mind
is on other things,

1097
01:54:35,915 --> 01:54:38,633
like that
silly little girl.

1098
01:54:49,996 --> 01:54:54,199
What's she like—
my rival?

1099
01:54:59,021 --> 01:55:01,206
Your kind of girl,
I bet.

1100
01:55:03,993 --> 01:55:06,594
Doe-eyed and obedient.
A little bit bland.

1101
01:55:08,131 --> 01:55:10,431
Please give it back to me.
It's all I've got.

1102
01:55:10,500 --> 01:55:13,100
It's all
you've got?

1103
01:55:13,169 --> 01:55:15,653
It's all you've got?
I laid out everything for you.

1104
01:55:15,721 --> 01:55:18,606
I pampered you, and that's
what you say to me?

1105
01:55:18,675 --> 01:55:21,826
Do you have any idea
how insulting that is?

1106
01:55:25,632 --> 01:55:29,033
Never mind.

1107
01:55:29,102 --> 01:55:32,970
I'm going away tomorrow
to start my work again,

1108
01:55:33,040 --> 01:55:36,690
bring a little snow
on the mountaintops,

1109
01:55:36,759 --> 01:55:38,459
remind people
winter's coming.

1110
01:55:38,528 --> 01:55:40,395
Give it back.

1111
01:55:40,463 --> 01:55:42,530
Come up and see me when you're
ready for that second kiss.

1112
01:55:58,331 --> 01:56:01,215
That was lovely.

1113
01:56:01,284 --> 01:56:03,451
Everybody,
wasn't it?

1114
01:56:06,272 --> 01:56:08,105
You... you watched
my dream?

1115
01:56:08,174 --> 01:56:11,392
Of course.
It was wonderful.

1116
01:56:11,460 --> 01:56:12,894
That's spying.

1117
01:56:12,962 --> 01:56:16,264
Didn't you watch my dreams
that first night?

1118
01:56:16,332 --> 01:56:17,731
And didn't you
promise me

1119
01:56:17,801 --> 01:56:20,401
you'd tell me where to find
the Snow Queen's palace?

1120
01:56:20,469 --> 01:56:23,771
And all you've done
is try to keep me here.

1121
01:56:23,840 --> 01:56:26,107
All the information
you need is here, dear,

1122
01:56:26,176 --> 01:56:27,975
and tonight,
it'll be yours.

1123
01:56:28,044 --> 01:56:29,293
No.

1124
01:56:29,362 --> 01:56:31,095
I have to find Kai.

1125
01:56:31,164 --> 01:56:36,334
But you have found him.
He's here, in your dreams,

1126
01:56:36,403 --> 01:56:41,339
whenever you wish,
and he'll always be perfect.

1127
01:56:41,408 --> 01:56:42,807
What could be
better than that?

1128
01:56:42,875 --> 01:56:45,976
This.

1129
01:56:46,045 --> 01:56:48,429
What you don't seem
to realize, dear,

1130
01:56:48,498 --> 01:56:50,064
is that i'm
quite serious

1131
01:56:50,133 --> 01:56:52,283
about finding
a husband for you.

1132
01:56:52,352 --> 01:56:56,087
Smart, beautiful assistant
wanting to leave palace?

1133
01:56:56,155 --> 01:56:58,356
Stay out of this,
conjurer.

1134
01:56:58,425 --> 01:56:59,557
It's no business
of yours.

1135
01:57:01,327 --> 01:57:03,610
Let's go.

1136
01:57:03,679 --> 01:57:07,031
Stop her!
Guards! Stop her!

1137
01:57:12,288 --> 01:57:15,857
Hey! Here I am.

1138
01:57:15,926 --> 01:57:18,092
There she is!
Forward!

1139
01:57:18,161 --> 01:57:19,827
This way!

1140
01:57:19,895 --> 01:57:21,729
Wow!

1141
01:57:21,797 --> 01:57:23,998
First time
that trick ever worked.

1142
01:57:25,468 --> 01:57:28,436
Thank you, Chen.
I'll never forget you.

1143
01:57:42,586 --> 01:57:48,089
I'm not sure the boy's going
to get the mirror finished,

1144
01:57:48,157 --> 01:57:49,991
not in time,
anyway.

1145
01:57:50,060 --> 01:57:53,311
Well, it's your job
to see that he does,

1146
01:57:53,380 --> 01:57:57,014
before the winter solstice.
Am I clear?

1147
01:57:57,083 --> 01:58:00,852
As ice.
I just don't see

1148
01:58:00,920 --> 01:58:03,271
why you're pinning
so much hope on this one.

1149
01:58:05,808 --> 01:58:08,443
Love.

1150
01:58:08,511 --> 01:58:11,379
True love.

1151
01:58:11,448 --> 01:58:14,148
Kai's seen it, felt it,

1152
01:58:14,217 --> 01:58:15,700
had it...

1153
01:58:15,769 --> 01:58:16,968
Has it.

1154
01:58:17,037 --> 01:58:19,203
He's not the only one.

1155
01:58:19,271 --> 01:58:20,571
What did you say?

1156
01:58:20,640 --> 01:58:24,025
Nothing.

1157
01:58:59,312 --> 01:59:00,478
Who are you?

1158
01:59:00,547 --> 01:59:02,346
The reason princesses
shouldn't go strolling about

1159
01:59:02,415 --> 01:59:06,333
alone in the forest,
my dear.

1160
01:59:06,402 --> 01:59:07,885
I'm not a Princess,

1161
01:59:07,954 --> 01:59:11,155
and I'll walk where I like,
thank you very much.

1162
01:59:11,223 --> 01:59:12,223
Get out of my way.

1163
01:59:12,291 --> 01:59:14,659
Oh, "get out
of my way," is it?

1164
01:59:14,727 --> 01:59:16,660
What do you think
about that, boys?

1165
01:59:16,729 --> 01:59:20,865
We think that's a bit
of a giggle, "robber girl."

1166
01:59:23,169 --> 01:59:24,168
Leave me alone.

1167
01:59:24,236 --> 01:59:26,820
Shut it, Princess.
You're coming with us.

1168
01:59:26,889 --> 01:59:28,021
Yes.

1169
01:59:41,437 --> 01:59:45,372
I'm the Summer Princess now.
Look at me.

1170
01:59:45,441 --> 01:59:47,491
What ransom
we're going to get.

1171
01:59:47,560 --> 01:59:49,560
Yes!
Come meet my mom.

1172
01:59:49,629 --> 01:59:54,348
Mom! The Princess
is here.

1173
01:59:54,417 --> 01:59:57,785
What have you
brought me today, girl?

1174
01:59:57,853 --> 01:59:59,687
Brought you
the Summer Princess.

1175
02:00:00,873 --> 02:00:03,240
What have you got
in your hand?

1176
02:00:04,377 --> 02:00:05,676
Give it
back to me.

1177
02:00:09,064 --> 02:00:13,267
Pretty—
but very sharp.

1178
02:00:13,336 --> 02:00:14,835
She's not
the Summer Princess.

1179
02:00:14,904 --> 02:00:16,504
She is!

1180
02:00:16,572 --> 02:00:18,022
She was in a complete
Summer Princess outfit.

1181
02:00:18,091 --> 02:00:20,891
She's right.
I'm just a poor, ordinary girl.

1182
02:00:20,960 --> 02:00:22,793
No one will pay
any ransom for me.

1183
02:00:22,862 --> 02:00:25,379
Might as well shove you
in the cooking pot, then.

1184
02:00:25,448 --> 02:00:27,682
Is the water boiling yet?

1185
02:00:28,818 --> 02:00:31,502
I've got quite a hunger
on me tonight.

1186
02:00:31,571 --> 02:00:33,204
She'll do just nicely.

1187
02:00:33,273 --> 02:00:35,289
And make sure
you add some onions!

1188
02:00:36,475 --> 02:00:39,443
The palace might pay something.
You never know.

1189
02:00:59,733 --> 02:01:01,432
You're not
cooking her.

1190
02:01:01,500 --> 02:01:04,168
What do you think you're doing?
That's my dinner.

1191
02:01:04,237 --> 02:01:05,953
No, I need a playmate.

1192
02:01:06,022 --> 02:01:08,405
There is no one
my own age to play with.

1193
02:01:08,474 --> 02:01:10,958
I always told you
not to play with your food.

1194
02:01:13,997 --> 02:01:15,496
Throw her in the pot.

1195
02:01:15,565 --> 02:01:19,817
I don't think I'll taste
that good... really.

1196
02:01:19,886 --> 02:01:22,270
I need
a peer group.

1197
02:01:22,338 --> 02:01:24,605
She's not a peer group.
She's supper.

1198
02:01:26,959 --> 02:01:28,892
So, can I keep her?

1199
02:01:30,146 --> 02:01:31,646
Do we have any rabbits?

1200
02:01:31,714 --> 02:01:33,314
Couple of sacks full.

1201
02:01:33,383 --> 02:01:36,333
All right,
you can have her.

1202
02:01:36,402 --> 02:01:37,952
We'll do a curry.

1203
02:01:38,021 --> 02:01:39,987
See if you can rustle up
some of that basmati rice.

1204
02:01:40,056 --> 02:01:41,939
There you are.

1205
02:01:42,007 --> 02:01:43,574
I didn't let them
kill you, did I?

1206
02:01:43,642 --> 02:01:47,778
If I get cross with you,
I'll do it myself.

1207
02:01:47,846 --> 02:01:51,382
Go on.
There's nothing to it.

1208
02:01:52,318 --> 02:01:54,151
Come on.

1209
02:02:32,075 --> 02:02:34,942
You must have robbed
a lot of people.

1210
02:02:35,011 --> 02:02:37,812
Oh, they deserved it.

1211
02:02:37,880 --> 02:02:40,998
The former owner of this hat
was a pompous twit.

1212
02:02:43,870 --> 02:02:47,504
That hat suits you.

1213
02:02:47,573 --> 02:02:51,742
I'm not sure if I believe
in stealing things...

1214
02:02:51,811 --> 02:02:53,244
Or killing people.

1215
02:02:53,313 --> 02:02:55,780
I don't believe in it, either.
I just do it.

1216
02:02:57,500 --> 02:02:59,584
Want an apple?

1217
02:03:04,323 --> 02:03:06,723
Don't worry,

1218
02:03:06,792 --> 02:03:08,325
I'll teach you
everything I know.

1219
02:03:08,394 --> 02:03:10,795
Then, when something
comes along in life
that you want,

1220
02:03:10,863 --> 02:03:13,613
you'll be able to take it,
just like that.

1221
02:03:15,217 --> 02:03:16,317
Come on,
time for bed.

1222
02:04:38,284 --> 02:04:40,468
I knew you'd be back.

1223
02:05:05,828 --> 02:05:08,729
Dance, damn you!

1224
02:05:10,549 --> 02:05:11,715
Come on, dance!

1225
02:05:25,147 --> 02:05:28,749
I want real dancing,
like...

1226
02:05:28,818 --> 02:05:32,336
The conga!
Yes, that's what I want!

1227
02:05:36,559 --> 02:05:38,158
She's getting uppity,
the robber girl.

1228
02:05:38,227 --> 02:05:40,193
There's nothing wrong
with my daughter.

1229
02:05:40,262 --> 02:05:42,863
She's a fine girl
in a fine robbing tradition.

1230
02:05:42,932 --> 02:05:44,998
She spat in your eye
today, didn't she?

1231
02:05:45,067 --> 02:05:48,569
Shows she's got
what it takes, that's all.

1232
02:05:48,638 --> 02:05:50,571
You're gonna
put up with that?

1233
02:05:50,640 --> 02:05:53,808
All right,
now through the fire,

1234
02:05:53,876 --> 02:05:56,510
not just around it.
Through the fire.

1235
02:08:34,770 --> 02:08:36,570
I trusted you.

1236
02:08:36,638 --> 02:08:37,604
I knew you'd
let me down.

1237
02:08:37,673 --> 02:08:39,673
Everyone does!

1238
02:08:39,742 --> 02:08:41,675
I ought to slit
your throat.

1239
02:08:41,744 --> 02:08:43,961
Exactly what I'd hoped
you'd say, girl.

1240
02:08:44,030 --> 02:08:48,115
You're growing up.
Go on, do it.

1241
02:08:48,184 --> 02:08:50,017
I ought to
cut off your head,

1242
02:08:50,086 --> 02:08:52,886
and use it
for a football.

1243
02:08:52,954 --> 02:08:56,156
That's the spirit.
Come on, lads, form two teams.

1244
02:08:56,225 --> 02:08:58,358
We're going
to have a game.

1245
02:08:58,427 --> 02:09:01,779
Teamwork, essence
of good robbing.

1246
02:09:05,167 --> 02:09:07,384
Want to borrow this?

1247
02:09:07,453 --> 02:09:10,771
Make a nice,
clean job of it?

1248
02:09:10,840 --> 02:09:12,807
No thank you, mom.

1249
02:09:12,875 --> 02:09:14,608
I have my own way
of dealing with this.

1250
02:09:16,245 --> 02:09:18,912
What are you going to do,
saw it off?

1251
02:09:18,981 --> 02:09:20,547
Good idea.

1252
02:09:20,616 --> 02:09:23,517
Teach her a lesson
she won't forget.

1253
02:09:23,586 --> 02:09:26,487
If you don't
want to be with me,
you can be in our jail.

1254
02:09:31,393 --> 02:09:35,295
I hate you!
You can rot there forever!

1255
02:09:49,895 --> 02:09:52,629
You've really
disappointed them,
you know that?

1256
02:09:52,698 --> 02:09:57,167
They were really looking forward
to a bit of clean, healthy fun,

1257
02:09:57,236 --> 02:09:59,436
and you've just spoiled it.

1258
02:09:59,505 --> 02:10:01,304
Tcha!

1259
02:10:05,077 --> 02:10:07,778
Anybody fancy
some mah-jongg?

1260
02:10:07,847 --> 02:10:09,847
Roulette?

1261
02:10:09,915 --> 02:10:12,315
Russian roulette?

1262
02:10:12,385 --> 02:10:15,218
Yeah!

1263
02:10:28,567 --> 02:10:30,584
Mr. Mayor, tell him
he can't do that.

1264
02:10:30,653 --> 02:10:32,552
What do you think
you're up to, Wolfgang?

1265
02:10:32,621 --> 02:10:36,206
I'm closing up
the white bear hotel,
that's what I'm up to.

1266
02:10:36,275 --> 02:10:38,775
But you can't, Wolfgang.
You can't do that.

1267
02:10:38,844 --> 02:10:41,528
I can.

1268
02:10:41,597 --> 02:10:44,564
I don't care if I
never see a guest
as long as I live.

1269
02:10:44,633 --> 02:10:47,718
But think of the town, Wolfgang.
Think what this means
to the town.

1270
02:10:47,787 --> 02:10:49,954
I don't care
about the town,

1271
02:10:50,022 --> 02:10:52,656
I don't care
about this hotel,

1272
02:10:52,725 --> 02:10:54,191
and I don't care
about you...

1273
02:10:54,260 --> 02:10:55,525
Any of you.

1274
02:10:55,594 --> 02:11:00,247
Now, go away
and leave me alone.

1275
02:11:09,641 --> 02:11:11,241
Describe it.

1276
02:11:11,310 --> 02:11:13,877
I can't.

1277
02:11:13,946 --> 02:11:15,913
No, you can't.

1278
02:11:15,981 --> 02:11:18,598
Do you know what
winter is, Kai?

1279
02:11:18,667 --> 02:11:21,901
Winter is me.

1280
02:11:24,457 --> 02:11:28,042
What's happened
to me?

1281
02:11:28,110 --> 02:11:29,676
Everything looks
so perfect,

1282
02:11:29,745 --> 02:11:32,429
so mathematical.
I mean, look at this.

1283
02:11:32,498 --> 02:11:34,231
Perfect patterns,
perfect shapes.

1284
02:11:34,300 --> 02:11:37,501
It's nothing, Kai.
Even this,

1285
02:11:37,570 --> 02:11:39,035
everything you're feeling
in this moment,

1286
02:11:39,104 --> 02:11:41,288
this is just a snowflake
on an iceberg.

1287
02:11:41,357 --> 02:11:44,458
This is just the start
of your change.

1288
02:11:45,594 --> 02:11:47,828
We're at the end
of the world, Kai.

1289
02:11:47,897 --> 02:11:49,747
No one could
ever come here.

1290
02:11:49,815 --> 02:11:51,715
Just you and me.

1291
02:11:56,538 --> 02:11:59,339
Kiss me again.
I'm ready.

1292
02:11:59,408 --> 02:12:02,693
Would you like to ride
a storm with me?

1293
02:12:02,762 --> 02:12:06,279
Would you like to ride
on the wind and the snow?

1294
02:12:06,348 --> 02:12:10,918
You know what you could do,
now that you can see like this?

1295
02:12:10,987 --> 02:12:12,886
Tell me.
I'll do anything.

1296
02:12:12,955 --> 02:12:16,789
You can finish
the little mirror puzzle.

1297
02:12:16,858 --> 02:12:19,993
I bet you could do it in a month
if you didn't sleep.

1298
02:12:20,062 --> 02:12:21,862
A month?

1299
02:12:21,931 --> 02:12:24,197
I could stay awake
for a year.

1300
02:12:38,380 --> 02:12:40,564
I've told you
a thousand times,

1301
02:12:40,633 --> 02:12:42,899
you don't actually have
to Rob on your first time.

1302
02:12:42,968 --> 02:12:43,933
You can just watch.

1303
02:12:44,002 --> 02:12:44,734
No.

1304
02:12:45,671 --> 02:12:48,105
Why not?

1305
02:12:48,174 --> 02:12:49,873
They'd kill us,
given half the chance.

1306
02:12:49,942 --> 02:12:52,676
How do you think I got his?
Shot at, I was.

1307
02:12:52,745 --> 02:12:54,310
No, you weren't.

1308
02:12:54,380 --> 02:12:56,045
I've seen you
without your eye patch.

1309
02:12:56,114 --> 02:12:58,382
There's nothing wrong
with your eye.

1310
02:12:58,450 --> 02:12:59,766
But I might
have been shot at.

1311
02:12:59,835 --> 02:13:01,451
Except that you
shot at them first?

1312
02:13:01,520 --> 02:13:02,786
Exactly.

1313
02:13:02,854 --> 02:13:04,571
I'm not going to go out
shooting at people,

1314
02:13:04,640 --> 02:13:07,540
just in case they shoot at me,
and wearing an eye patch

1315
02:13:07,609 --> 02:13:09,243
to make people
feel sorry for me.

1316
02:13:09,311 --> 02:13:12,029
What about the benefits?
I mean, the proceeds?

1317
02:13:12,097 --> 02:13:14,864
Well, I'm sorry.
I'm not going to be a robber,

1318
02:13:14,933 --> 02:13:18,368
and that's that.
I have to find Kai.

1319
02:13:18,437 --> 02:13:21,621
The boy?
The boy who left you?

1320
02:13:21,690 --> 02:13:25,359
He didn't leave me.
The Snow Queen took him.

1321
02:13:25,427 --> 02:13:28,278
She didn't take him.
He left.

1322
02:13:28,347 --> 02:13:33,083
He went off with another woman.
An older woman at that.

1323
02:13:33,152 --> 02:13:35,118
Trailing on after him,
like a lovesick calf?

1324
02:13:35,187 --> 02:13:37,054
I have to rescue him.

1325
02:13:37,122 --> 02:13:38,922
How do you know
he wants rescuing?

1326
02:13:38,991 --> 02:13:40,457
Because I love him.

1327
02:13:40,525 --> 02:13:43,093
Because he loves me.

1328
02:13:44,814 --> 02:13:47,664
If he loves you,
then why did he go off with her?

1329
02:13:47,733 --> 02:13:50,184
She hardened his heart.

1330
02:13:50,252 --> 02:13:53,786
And you think you can
soften it, do you?

1331
02:13:53,855 --> 02:13:56,306
I will try.

1332
02:13:57,943 --> 02:14:01,861
Have you any idea how powerful
the Snow Queen really is?

1333
02:14:01,931 --> 02:14:07,351
Have you any idea how cruel,
and cold, and wonderful

1334
02:14:07,419 --> 02:14:08,952
she can be?

1335
02:14:09,021 --> 02:14:10,821
How can you even think
you can stand up to her?

1336
02:14:10,889 --> 02:14:13,741
Because I love him,
that's why.

1337
02:14:13,809 --> 02:14:15,809
With all my heart.

1338
02:14:15,878 --> 02:14:18,528
Well, you're kidding yourself,

1339
02:14:18,597 --> 02:14:20,630
and I'm going to make sure
you stop kidding yourself,

1340
02:14:20,699 --> 02:14:22,899
and you stay here
until you see sense,

1341
02:14:22,968 --> 02:14:25,802
and take up a useful career,
like robbing.

1342
02:14:36,048 --> 02:14:37,180
Do we have to
just tap,

1343
02:14:37,249 --> 02:14:39,416
or can we talk
as well?

1344
02:14:39,485 --> 02:14:41,718
Who's in there?

1345
02:14:41,786 --> 02:14:44,888
I'm rutger.
Who are you?

1346
02:14:44,956 --> 02:14:47,657
Gerda.
Are you in a cell as well?

1347
02:14:47,726 --> 02:14:51,378
No. I'm in a shed.
I can see the daylight.

1348
02:14:51,447 --> 02:14:52,446
I could escape,

1349
02:14:52,514 --> 02:14:54,781
if only I wasn't
chained to the wall.

1350
02:14:54,850 --> 02:14:56,149
How long have you
been in there?

1351
02:14:56,218 --> 02:14:58,751
I'm not sure.
I think about two years.

1352
02:14:58,820 --> 02:15:00,186
No...

1353
02:15:00,255 --> 02:15:03,823
Oh, yes. Once they catch you,
they never let you go.

1354
02:15:03,892 --> 02:15:05,725
If only I could
get to you...

1355
02:15:05,794 --> 02:15:08,194
You could unchain me,
and then we can get out.

1356
02:15:08,263 --> 02:15:09,796
I could kick
the door down.

1357
02:15:09,864 --> 02:15:12,432
Kick your way out?
Do you really think so?

1358
02:15:12,500 --> 02:15:16,403
Well, we have to look
on the bright side,
don't we?

1359
02:15:38,510 --> 02:15:42,044
They're all different.
That's the amazing thing.

1360
02:15:44,449 --> 02:15:48,084
Why did I have trouble
distinguishing between them?

1361
02:15:56,361 --> 02:16:00,296
Each one of them
has its own personality.

1362
02:16:00,365 --> 02:16:02,899
I can see the patterns.

1363
02:16:02,967 --> 02:16:06,969
I can see the patterns
before my eyes.

1364
02:16:07,038 --> 02:16:09,539
Oh, I meant
to ask you,

1365
02:16:09,608 --> 02:16:13,359
do you remember that girl
you used to talk about?

1366
02:16:13,428 --> 02:16:15,562
I do, yes.

1367
02:16:15,631 --> 02:16:17,264
You're sure?

1368
02:16:17,333 --> 02:16:19,599
Yes.

1369
02:16:19,668 --> 02:16:23,370
Remind me...
What did she look like?

1370
02:16:23,438 --> 02:16:27,841
I wouldn't call her ugly,
but, a boy like you,

1371
02:16:27,909 --> 02:16:30,711
you're one in a million.
You deserve the best.

1372
02:16:30,779 --> 02:16:32,412
And that's you.

1373
02:16:33,649 --> 02:16:36,132
Why don't you show him
the others?

1374
02:16:38,036 --> 02:16:40,637
You don't want him
to like me, bear?

1375
02:16:43,125 --> 02:16:44,057
Well?

1376
02:16:44,126 --> 02:16:46,943
You know I don't.

1377
02:16:47,011 --> 02:16:48,811
And why would that be?

1378
02:16:48,880 --> 02:16:50,897
You know the answer to that,
as well.

1379
02:16:50,965 --> 02:16:52,965
But I like to hear it.

1380
02:16:53,034 --> 02:16:56,153
Be— because
I love you.

1381
02:16:56,221 --> 02:17:01,240
What was that?
I didn't quite catch that.

1382
02:17:01,309 --> 02:17:03,159
Because
I love you.

1383
02:17:03,228 --> 02:17:06,897
Because you love me.
How wonderfully absurd.

1384
02:17:06,965 --> 02:17:09,115
He loves me.

1385
02:17:13,388 --> 02:17:15,788
You're not like the other boys,
are you, Kai?

1386
02:17:15,857 --> 02:17:18,508
Not at all.

1387
02:17:18,576 --> 02:17:20,961
They were
just pieces.

1388
02:17:34,742 --> 02:17:37,577
She's gotten
far too big for her boots.

1389
02:17:37,645 --> 02:17:40,980
She needs taking down
a peg or two,

1390
02:17:41,049 --> 02:17:45,851
before the whole year
is covered with snow.

1391
02:18:03,188 --> 02:18:06,390
All my frozen
failures.

1392
02:18:40,408 --> 02:18:42,708
There's magic in this.

1393
02:18:42,777 --> 02:18:44,327
I want to know about it.

1394
02:18:44,395 --> 02:18:47,563
It was my mother's,
and now it's mine.

1395
02:18:47,633 --> 02:18:49,032
It's mine.

1396
02:18:49,101 --> 02:18:50,884
You've got it,

1397
02:18:50,953 --> 02:18:54,020
but it's not yours,
and it never will be.

1398
02:18:54,089 --> 02:18:55,488
Is that so?

1399
02:18:55,557 --> 02:18:58,908
It's the only thing I have
of hers, and she's dead,

1400
02:18:58,977 --> 02:19:02,094
so I think you should
give it back to me.

1401
02:19:02,163 --> 02:19:03,663
People die
all the time.

1402
02:19:03,732 --> 02:19:05,465
They blaze red

1403
02:19:05,534 --> 02:19:07,617
as if they're going
to live forever,

1404
02:19:07,686 --> 02:19:09,986
but they all fall
sooner or later.

1405
02:19:10,055 --> 02:19:11,888
There's nothing
you can do about it.

1406
02:19:11,957 --> 02:19:15,058
People don't come back
because we want them to...

1407
02:19:15,126 --> 02:19:16,709
Princess.

1408
02:19:16,779 --> 02:19:18,711
The world moves on.

1409
02:19:18,781 --> 02:19:21,414
Even I can't stop the leaves
from falling.

1410
02:19:21,483 --> 02:19:23,616
I know she won't
come back,

1411
02:19:23,685 --> 02:19:27,387
but I just want to keep
a piece of her with me.

1412
02:19:27,455 --> 02:19:29,956
Wouldn't you want your daughter
to keep hold

1413
02:19:30,025 --> 02:19:32,492
of something of yours
when you're gone?

1414
02:19:32,560 --> 02:19:35,428
There's heat
in this brooch.

1415
02:19:35,497 --> 02:19:38,531
That's what she fears,
you know.

1416
02:19:39,968 --> 02:19:44,237
The one you want to see.
The one who's got your man.

1417
02:19:45,390 --> 02:19:47,390
Do you know her?

1418
02:19:47,459 --> 02:19:51,444
Know her?
She's my sister.

1419
02:19:55,667 --> 02:19:59,202
But...
But she's a queen.

1420
02:19:59,271 --> 02:20:01,554
And I'm just
a robber, eh?

1421
02:20:01,622 --> 02:20:03,622
It shouldn't be like that,
should it?

1422
02:20:03,691 --> 02:20:06,726
Is it right?
Is it just?

1423
02:20:06,795 --> 02:20:09,329
Of course it isn't.

1424
02:20:09,397 --> 02:20:12,732
She's gotten far too powerful.

1425
02:20:12,800 --> 02:20:14,417
Yes.

1426
02:20:14,486 --> 02:20:18,288
She needs taking down
a peg or two.

1427
02:20:18,357 --> 02:20:20,840
But your daughter
said I wasn't strong enough.

1428
02:20:20,909 --> 02:20:22,875
What does she know?

1429
02:20:22,944 --> 02:20:25,796
Will you let me go?

1430
02:20:25,864 --> 02:20:29,966
Will you let me go find her,
so I can go save Kai?

1431
02:20:30,035 --> 02:20:32,451
You are no threat
to her.

1432
02:20:32,520 --> 02:20:34,387
But she'd never
forgive me.

1433
02:20:34,456 --> 02:20:38,608
Who, the robber girl?
Of course she will—
you're her mother.

1434
02:20:38,677 --> 02:20:41,994
You think girls
ever forgive their mothers?

1435
02:20:42,063 --> 02:20:44,147
Of course not.

1436
02:21:11,893 --> 02:21:14,527
Please help me, mother.

1437
02:21:14,596 --> 02:21:18,698
Please help me to find Kai,
and get him back.

1438
02:21:46,127 --> 02:21:48,561
Keep going,
keep going.

1439
02:21:48,630 --> 02:21:50,329
I can see
the wall buckling.

1440
02:21:50,398 --> 02:21:51,464
It's hard.

1441
02:21:51,533 --> 02:21:53,867
I know it's hard,
but believe me,

1442
02:21:53,935 --> 02:21:56,485
when you're through,
it'll be worth it.

1443
02:21:56,554 --> 02:21:58,888
Who's that?
Who are you talking to?

1444
02:21:58,957 --> 02:22:00,990
Myself.

1445
02:22:01,058 --> 02:22:03,593
I'm talking to myself
because I'm lonely.

1446
02:22:05,530 --> 02:22:07,230
You can come out
whenever you want,

1447
02:22:07,298 --> 02:22:09,866
as soon as you agree
to join the band.

1448
02:22:09,935 --> 02:22:11,067
No!

1449
02:22:11,136 --> 02:22:13,519
Fine.
Stay there and rot.

1450
02:22:13,588 --> 02:22:14,954
We're having
paella tonight,

1451
02:22:15,023 --> 02:22:16,573
and you're not going
to get any.

1452
02:22:16,641 --> 02:22:18,324
Stolen paella.

1453
02:22:18,393 --> 02:22:20,076
Still tastes
delicious, though.

1454
02:22:20,144 --> 02:22:21,644
Let me know
when you want to come out,

1455
02:22:21,713 --> 02:22:24,781
and you can get some.

1456
02:22:56,515 --> 02:22:58,998
Well, hello.

1457
02:23:01,752 --> 02:23:04,854
I... I thought
you were a person.

1458
02:23:04,922 --> 02:23:07,223
No, more
of a reindeer, really.

1459
02:23:07,292 --> 02:23:08,991
It's the antlers,
you know.

1460
02:23:09,060 --> 02:23:13,647
You wouldn't by any chance
have any acorns on you, hmm?

1461
02:23:29,514 --> 02:23:32,215
Is anyone going to do anything
about breakfast?

1462
02:23:39,223 --> 02:23:40,723
Hey, watch your head.
Watch your head!

1463
02:23:54,439 --> 02:23:56,706
Winter's almost here.

1464
02:23:56,775 --> 02:23:59,909
I can see the snow
on top of the hills.

1465
02:23:59,978 --> 02:24:02,294
Good for sledging.

1466
02:24:08,669 --> 02:24:11,604
Wonderful,
having hands.

1467
02:24:11,673 --> 02:24:14,724
Hooves aren't much use
for that kind of thing.

1468
02:24:14,793 --> 02:24:17,060
No, but they'll be good
to race away from here

1469
02:24:17,128 --> 02:24:19,261
faster than the wind,
when we get out of here.

1470
02:24:20,732 --> 02:24:22,014
Do you know the way
to lapland?

1471
02:24:22,083 --> 02:24:27,353
Lapland?
Like the back of my antlers.

1472
02:24:27,406 --> 02:24:29,672
I need to find the Snow Queen
before the winter solstice.

1473
02:24:29,741 --> 02:24:31,941
Yes, I think I can
get you there in time.

1474
02:24:32,009 --> 02:24:35,544
I think we should run through
huge zigzags through the forest,

1475
02:24:35,613 --> 02:24:37,513
so the robbers won't know
which way we're going to go.

1476
02:24:37,582 --> 02:24:41,500
Zigzags, yes,
but not the running, of course,

1477
02:24:41,569 --> 02:24:44,904
not at my age.
Have you ever had arthritis?

1478
02:24:44,973 --> 02:24:46,856
But why did I spend
all of this effort,

1479
02:24:46,925 --> 02:24:48,525
digging through
this wall if—

1480
02:24:48,593 --> 02:24:50,777
there was
just a poor old reindeer

1481
02:24:50,846 --> 02:24:54,013
on the other side,
hoping you'd help him?

1482
02:24:54,082 --> 02:24:58,150
I'm sorry.
That was very selfish of me.

1483
02:24:59,320 --> 02:25:00,870
I'm very glad to have
met you, rutger

1484
02:25:00,938 --> 02:25:05,024
even if you do have
some... mobility problems.

1485
02:25:09,364 --> 02:25:10,663
How very touching.

1486
02:25:10,732 --> 02:25:11,948
Uh-oh!

1487
02:25:14,068 --> 02:25:16,135
You were about to steal
my reindeer.

1488
02:25:16,204 --> 02:25:17,670
Not too many scruples
about robbing

1489
02:25:17,739 --> 02:25:20,089
when it comes to something
you actually want, huh?

1490
02:25:20,158 --> 02:25:21,757
This is completely
different.

1491
02:25:21,810 --> 02:25:24,677
In fact, if you think
robbing's so fine,

1492
02:25:24,745 --> 02:25:26,879
you'll have no problem
with me robbing you.

1493
02:25:26,948 --> 02:25:30,482
Ooh— saucy.
Well take that, saucy girl.

1494
02:25:33,555 --> 02:25:35,137
Nobody steals
from the robber girl,

1495
02:25:35,207 --> 02:25:37,139
and nobody gets away
from the robber girl,

1496
02:25:37,209 --> 02:25:40,326
or they feel... this.

1497
02:25:42,313 --> 02:25:45,265
Or not, depending
on the reindeer.

1498
02:25:45,333 --> 02:25:47,850
What do you think you're doing,
you rheumatic old fool?

1499
02:25:47,902 --> 02:25:49,385
Fighting for freedom.

1500
02:25:55,143 --> 02:25:57,226
What do you think
you're doing?

1501
02:25:57,294 --> 02:25:59,295
What you taught me to do,
robber girl.

1502
02:25:59,364 --> 02:26:00,830
Standing up for myself.

1503
02:26:00,898 --> 02:26:02,565
Standing up
for yourself?

1504
02:26:02,634 --> 02:26:05,485
Yes. You only think
about what you want,

1505
02:26:05,553 --> 02:26:07,787
and now I'm going to think
about what I want,

1506
02:26:07,856 --> 02:26:11,340
and that's to get out
of here, and find Kai.

1507
02:26:20,751 --> 02:26:22,135
Mommy!

1508
02:26:22,203 --> 02:26:24,403
Mommy!

1509
02:26:25,339 --> 02:26:26,940
Faster, rutger.

1510
02:26:27,008 --> 02:26:29,108
This is faster.

1511
02:26:42,974 --> 02:26:46,809
Clever boy.

1512
02:26:46,877 --> 02:26:50,313
No one's ever gotten close
to what you've done.

1513
02:26:50,381 --> 02:26:53,816
I knew when I first saw you
that you were special.

1514
02:26:53,885 --> 02:26:57,486
It's magnificent,
and I applaud you.

1515
02:26:57,555 --> 02:27:00,089
To come so close...

1516
02:27:00,158 --> 02:27:02,391
What do you mean, "so close"?
It's complete.

1517
02:27:04,896 --> 02:27:06,695
I've done what you've
asked me to do.

1518
02:27:06,765 --> 02:27:09,848
Maybe there's something
wrong with my eyesight,

1519
02:27:09,917 --> 02:27:13,118
but there seems to be
one piece missing.

1520
02:27:13,188 --> 02:27:14,720
Where is it?

1521
02:27:14,789 --> 02:27:17,807
I've looked everywhere.

1522
02:27:20,879 --> 02:27:26,265
You've hidden it from me,
haven't you?

1523
02:27:26,334 --> 02:27:29,135
Because that's all there is,
all right? It's not there.

1524
02:27:30,621 --> 02:27:32,755
You're not quite ready
for that last kiss.

1525
02:27:32,824 --> 02:27:34,357
You haven't
worked it out yet.

1526
02:27:40,265 --> 02:27:41,297
It's not here.

1527
02:27:41,366 --> 02:27:43,299
I've looked
for three days.

1528
02:27:43,368 --> 02:27:46,069
I've crawled
on my hands and knees.

1529
02:27:46,137 --> 02:27:48,086
I can see everything
in this room,

1530
02:27:48,155 --> 02:27:49,388
every tiny speck.
It's not here.

1531
02:27:49,457 --> 02:27:50,989
It is here.

1532
02:27:51,058 --> 02:27:53,776
It's not!

1533
02:27:57,616 --> 02:27:59,816
Why can't I finish
the puzzle?

1534
02:28:02,236 --> 02:28:04,403
You're not going
to like the answer.

1535
02:28:41,292 --> 02:28:43,142
Listen.

1536
02:28:43,211 --> 02:28:44,927
What?

1537
02:28:44,996 --> 02:28:47,080
The story
is being told.

1538
02:28:47,148 --> 02:28:49,715
Can you hear it
on the wind?

1539
02:28:51,186 --> 02:28:53,635
<i> Thousands and thousands</i>
<i> of years ago,</i>

1540
02:28:53,704 --> 02:28:57,489
<i> deep down in hell... </i>

1541
02:28:59,361 --> 02:29:03,062
<i> The devil</i>
<i> made a mirror.</i>

1542
02:29:29,173 --> 02:29:32,341
The devil gave this
beautiful mirror

1543
02:29:32,427 --> 02:29:34,059
to the four seasons,

1544
02:29:34,128 --> 02:29:37,529
<i> so that they could</i>
<i> admire their work,</i>

1545
02:29:37,598 --> 02:29:41,317
<i> and when the spring</i>
<i> stood in front of the mirror,</i>

1546
02:29:41,385 --> 02:29:44,203
<i> it reflected the essence</i>
<i> of her season,</i>

1547
02:29:44,272 --> 02:29:46,505
<i> and the promise of life.</i>

1548
02:29:46,574 --> 02:29:49,075
<i> And so it was for summer... </i>

1549
02:29:50,478 --> 02:29:52,111
<i> And autumn.</i>

1550
02:29:52,180 --> 02:29:55,464
<i> And when the winter</i>
<i> stood in front of the mirror,</i>

1551
02:29:55,533 --> 02:29:59,451
<i> the world was reflected</i>
<i> cold and covered in snow,</i>

1552
02:29:59,520 --> 02:30:01,153
<i> and that was</i>
<i> as it should be,</i>

1553
02:30:01,222 --> 02:30:03,372
<i> for each season</i>
<i> has its power and its time,</i>

1554
02:30:03,441 --> 02:30:06,358
<i> and there was harmony.</i>

1555
02:30:06,427 --> 02:30:10,112
<i> But the devil</i>
<i> had made the mirror twisted,</i>

1556
02:30:10,181 --> 02:30:12,748
so that as winter gazed
at her own face,

1557
02:30:12,817 --> 02:30:16,618
she longed to be queen
of the seasons,

1558
02:30:16,687 --> 02:30:19,354
<i> and one day</i>
<i> she stole the mirror,</i>

1559
02:30:19,423 --> 02:30:22,074
<i> and took it to the arctic</i>
<i> wastes for herself.</i>

1560
02:30:22,143 --> 02:30:25,527
<i> Now she was</i>
<i> the Snow Queen,</i>

1561
02:30:25,596 --> 02:30:28,397
<i> and the world</i>
<i> became a colder place,</i>

1562
02:30:28,466 --> 02:30:30,649
but not cold
enough for her,

1563
02:30:30,718 --> 02:30:34,086
<i> because autumn, and spring,</i>
<i> and summer still existed,</i>

1564
02:30:34,155 --> 02:30:37,189
<i> however diminished,</i>
<i> so she took the mirror,</i>

1565
02:30:37,258 --> 02:30:39,491
and flew with it
up into the sky

1566
02:30:41,045 --> 02:30:45,515
that winter should rule
the earth, unchallenged.

1567
02:30:48,169 --> 02:30:50,670
<i> But as she</i>
<i> approached heaven,</i>

1568
02:30:50,738 --> 02:30:52,888
<i> the mirror</i>
<i> shook and shook,</i>

1569
02:30:52,957 --> 02:30:54,490
<i> as if good and evil</i>

1570
02:30:54,559 --> 02:30:57,043
<i> were wrestling</i>
<i> for control.</i>

1571
02:30:57,111 --> 02:30:59,645
<i> When the pieces</i>
<i> fell to earth,</i>

1572
02:30:59,714 --> 02:31:01,947
<i> and flew round</i>
<i> and round,</i>

1573
02:31:02,016 --> 02:31:03,882
<i> until they flew</i>
<i> into people's eyes—</i>

1574
02:31:03,951 --> 02:31:06,452
when those people
looked at the world,

1575
02:31:06,521 --> 02:31:09,421
they saw it as cold
and ugly,

1576
02:31:09,474 --> 02:31:13,809
and each winter,
she began to roam the earth,

1577
02:31:13,877 --> 02:31:18,848
looking for all
the missing pieces,

1578
02:31:18,916 --> 02:31:22,451
that one day she'd be able
to put the mirror back together,

1579
02:31:22,520 --> 02:31:24,787
and again become
all-powerful.

1580
02:31:26,190 --> 02:31:29,975
So you see why you can't
finish the puzzle?

1581
02:31:30,044 --> 02:31:31,427
Hmm?

1582
02:31:39,037 --> 02:31:41,654
Kai?

1583
02:31:41,723 --> 02:31:43,489
Kai, are you
all right?

1584
02:31:46,593 --> 02:31:48,794
It's inside me.

1585
02:31:48,862 --> 02:31:50,695
I'm
the missing piece.

1586
02:32:04,929 --> 02:32:08,163
How can I ever leave,
if I can't complete the mirror?

1587
02:32:08,233 --> 02:32:10,850
You can't.

1588
02:32:10,918 --> 02:32:14,070
How do I get it
out of me?

1589
02:32:14,138 --> 02:32:17,706
Just one
last kiss.

1590
02:32:17,775 --> 02:32:19,758
We're too late.

1591
02:32:19,827 --> 02:32:20,926
I'm never
going to be able

1592
02:32:20,995 --> 02:32:22,995
to get you there
in time.

1593
02:32:23,064 --> 02:32:25,597
Yes, you can,
I know it.

1594
02:32:25,666 --> 02:32:31,370
Gerda, I'm sorry.
I'm just... too old.

1595
02:32:31,438 --> 02:32:33,188
It's just over
those mountains.

1596
02:32:33,257 --> 02:32:36,975
Do you think you can
get there without me?

1597
02:32:39,063 --> 02:32:41,264
Nothing's going to stop me,
rutger.

1598
02:32:47,154 --> 02:32:49,187
So long, Gerda.

1599
02:34:50,044 --> 02:34:52,194
No, please.

1600
02:34:52,263 --> 02:34:54,730
Please what?
"Please don't kill me"?

1601
02:34:54,799 --> 02:34:57,883
No. Please let me
take Kai away.

1602
02:34:57,951 --> 02:34:59,334
Why should I do that?

1603
02:34:59,403 --> 02:35:01,387
Because I love him.

1604
02:35:01,456 --> 02:35:04,005
Why should I care
about that?

1605
02:35:04,075 --> 02:35:06,341
Don't you love
anybody?

1606
02:35:37,074 --> 02:35:39,741
Kai?

1607
02:35:41,195 --> 02:35:42,294
Kai!

1608
02:35:42,363 --> 02:35:44,430
Kai...

1609
02:35:46,200 --> 02:35:49,117
Kai...

1610
02:35:49,187 --> 02:35:51,720
Who are you?

1611
02:36:01,715 --> 02:36:03,782
What's happened to you?

1612
02:36:06,069 --> 02:36:08,470
What's happened
to your eyes?

1613
02:36:10,441 --> 02:36:14,043
You must remember me.
You must.

1614
02:36:14,111 --> 02:36:17,129
Please go,
before she finds you here.

1615
02:36:17,198 --> 02:36:19,164
No...

1616
02:36:19,233 --> 02:36:21,566
I've come to take you
home with me.

1617
02:36:21,635 --> 02:36:24,286
You must remember me.

1618
02:36:25,739 --> 02:36:29,141
I'm sorry, I don't seem
to know anything anymore.

1619
02:36:36,099 --> 02:36:40,402
Those boots...
I know those boots.

1620
02:36:40,471 --> 02:36:42,704
Yes.

1621
02:36:44,224 --> 02:36:45,290
I bought them.

1622
02:36:45,359 --> 02:36:47,026
Yes, yes, you did.

1623
02:36:49,112 --> 02:36:51,414
For you.

1624
02:36:55,670 --> 02:36:57,169
Gerda.

1625
02:36:57,237 --> 02:36:59,955
Yes.

1626
02:37:06,496 --> 02:37:07,963
I gave up hope.

1627
02:37:25,065 --> 02:37:26,598
What's wrong?

1628
02:37:26,667 --> 02:37:28,533
I feel so cold.

1629
02:37:30,488 --> 02:37:32,254
Where are you?

1630
02:37:33,591 --> 02:37:37,559
Where are you?
Stop doing this!

1631
02:37:44,252 --> 02:37:45,451
Please don't tell me
you thought

1632
02:37:45,520 --> 02:37:47,903
I'd let her just
come in here and take you,

1633
02:37:47,972 --> 02:37:52,057
because that would be such
an insult to my intelligence.

1634
02:37:55,529 --> 02:37:58,063
Stop it. She's dying.

1635
02:37:58,131 --> 02:38:01,633
I will stop,
and I'll let her live.

1636
02:38:01,702 --> 02:38:06,972
All you have to do
is kiss me a third time.

1637
02:38:08,709 --> 02:38:09,875
No.

1638
02:38:09,943 --> 02:38:15,347
I don't want her.
I want you.

1639
02:38:17,852 --> 02:38:19,985
What's more
important, Kai?

1640
02:38:20,053 --> 02:38:23,956
Your life
or hers?

1641
02:38:24,024 --> 02:38:27,025
One kiss from me
and she'll live.

1642
02:38:27,094 --> 02:38:32,681
Take all the time you want,
even though she's dying.

1643
02:38:41,609 --> 02:38:43,675
She's going, Kai...

1644
02:38:45,996 --> 02:38:49,765
Just like
her poor mother.

1645
02:38:55,940 --> 02:38:59,341
How well I remember
her last breath.

1646
02:39:06,967 --> 02:39:11,169
I'll do it.
Just don't kill her.

1647
02:39:12,089 --> 02:39:14,456
I knew you would.

1648
02:40:41,746 --> 02:40:44,930
Let the whole world
be as I am.

1649
02:40:47,434 --> 02:40:51,136
Let winter
rule always.

1650
02:40:51,204 --> 02:40:53,021
<i> Wake up.</i>

1651
02:40:53,090 --> 02:40:57,960
Wake up, sleepy girl,
wake up.

1652
02:40:58,029 --> 02:41:00,144
Wake up.
Come on, darling.

1653
02:41:00,213 --> 02:41:02,464
Come on, wake up!
Wake up!

1654
02:41:02,533 --> 02:41:03,464
You know what to do.

1655
02:41:03,533 --> 02:41:05,684
Wake up.
You know what to do.

1656
02:41:18,349 --> 02:41:22,166
Mommy's dead.

1657
02:41:22,235 --> 02:41:26,104
Get up, darling.

1658
02:41:31,362 --> 02:41:33,661
Mommy.

1659
02:41:34,898 --> 02:41:37,866
It's all right.

1660
02:41:37,935 --> 02:41:42,854
It's all right.

1661
02:41:45,926 --> 02:41:48,359
You don't have to cry
for me anymore.

1662
02:41:48,428 --> 02:41:51,212
It's time to move on.

1663
02:41:51,281 --> 02:41:54,499
You can do it.

1664
02:42:24,648 --> 02:42:27,365
What are you doing?
I froze you.

1665
02:42:29,353 --> 02:42:33,104
Oh, so you think
you're strong enough?

1666
02:42:33,173 --> 02:42:35,808
Such a fool.

1667
02:43:23,406 --> 02:43:27,475
Did you really think
you could take Kai away from me?

1668
02:43:30,664 --> 02:43:32,964
I'm the Snow Queen.

1669
02:43:34,501 --> 02:43:36,468
You're not
the Snow Queen.

1670
02:43:41,659 --> 02:43:44,092
You're just winter...

1671
02:43:59,793 --> 02:44:02,194
And winter passes.

1672
02:44:40,834 --> 02:44:43,235
It passes.

1673
02:44:46,940 --> 02:44:49,207
Kai, Kai...

1674
02:44:49,275 --> 02:44:52,644
I love you, Kai.

1675
02:44:52,713 --> 02:44:55,914
I love you.

1676
02:45:03,891 --> 02:45:08,277
What did you say?

1677
02:45:10,614 --> 02:45:13,014
I love you.

1678
02:45:15,118 --> 02:45:17,586
That's what
I thought it was.

1679
02:45:21,992 --> 02:45:25,794
Help me. Help me.

1680
02:45:28,165 --> 02:45:31,232
I can't stand.

1681
02:45:42,045 --> 02:45:44,178
It's all right.

1682
02:45:44,247 --> 02:45:48,966
It's all right.
I'm here.

1683
02:46:20,934 --> 02:46:23,001
Come on.

1684
02:47:14,822 --> 02:47:18,473
Gerda! Kai!

1685
02:47:18,542 --> 02:47:20,942
You came back.

1686
02:47:21,010 --> 02:47:22,977
I knew you would,
I knew you would.

1687
02:47:23,046 --> 02:47:25,463
Minna, it's so good
to see you again.

1688
02:47:25,532 --> 02:47:26,865
Where's Daddy?

1689
02:47:29,186 --> 02:47:31,603
Minna,
what happened?

1690
02:48:00,900 --> 02:48:04,018
Go away,
whoever you are.

1691
02:48:04,087 --> 02:48:08,006
Leave me alone.
I've told you often enough.

1692
02:48:08,075 --> 02:48:11,109
Daddy?

1693
02:48:11,177 --> 02:48:13,244
It's me, Gerda.

1694
02:48:13,313 --> 02:48:16,998
Daddy?

1695
02:48:17,067 --> 02:48:18,766
Not true.

1696
02:48:18,835 --> 02:48:24,422
Yes, Daddy,
it's true. I'm back.

1697
02:48:35,718 --> 02:48:38,136
Gerda!

1698
02:48:45,362 --> 02:48:46,978
I found Kai,
Daddy.

1699
02:48:47,046 --> 02:48:50,314
He's come back
with me.

1700
02:48:50,383 --> 02:48:53,184
We're never going to part
from one another again.

1701
02:49:46,088 --> 02:49:47,922
Tardiness of any
shape or form

1702
02:49:47,991 --> 02:49:51,092
will not be tolerated.
Now, get on with you!

1703
02:49:51,161 --> 02:49:52,527
Get!

